d conditional and one on the closure source — a mutant that reads `Winner.Checkpoint` again must die.\\nP2-1 — post-window same-pair race through `Run` reports `launch` with the winner's child. `Store.Supersede` replays the winner's receipt on the link `EEXIST` but returns no replay signal, and run.go:284-289 reports the decision unchanged: with a concurrent wrapper recording the same new pair between stage and link, the loser's outcome is `launch` with the WINNER's terminal instance while its own admitted descriptor names a different one. The in-window `Bind` path already flips this race to `reattach`; the post-window path must too. Make `Supersede` report replay (or compare the returned instance with the candidate), flip the outcome to `ActionReattach` with the recorded receipt, pin it through `Run` with the `Hooks.AfterStage` hook, and ship a narrowing mutant (a replay that keeps `launch`).\\nP3 — eight items, each named in the verdict with its probe or plant. Work them all, and note P3-3: the acceptance table has 43 rows and you publish 43/43, but the reviewer measures 39 of 43 because the four rows touching the post-takeover lifecycle are pinned to a refusal the spec does not require — once P1-1 is fixed those rows change meaning, so re-derive the ratio on the fixed tree and publish the number you measure.\\nAlso correct the prose the fix invalidates: the README sentence \\\"Resume derives the effective profile from the validated checkpoint's event-head closure\\\", the rev3 LOGBOOK F1 sentence \\\"a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\\\", and the matching TRACEABILITY rows.\\nProcedure: your candidate is on base 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91, which is current origin/main — do not refresh unless it actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-1geqhj` and audit every path in `git diff --name-only 2fc6d50 <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keeping README/LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content. You are a FIRST leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs), update TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and TASK-260830-1geqhj_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), reset and re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-1geqhj --role developer` so revision 4 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3 hours in — the scope is two sites and their evidence, not a rewrite.\\nPARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt of this run died to a provider idle timeout, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\\nCanonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 4.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 16019,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4005,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
