{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c505","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":221,"recorded_at":1780531400000437,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b195-a2a1-7273-8343-3d19e27ce972"},"task_id":"01a0b195-a2a1-7273-8343-3d19e27ce972","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b195-a2a1-7273-8343-3d19e27ce972","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-1geqhj-3 revision 3\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** One P1 class (two sites, one root cause), one P2, eight P3.\n4|\n5|Reviewer: RUN-260917-19551c (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n6|`2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91`, candidate tree\n7|`c0e8b422daa1d12f889174e1a92429f17416de90` (recomputed from the live Story\n8|worktree with an untracked-aware temporary index: equal), patch sha256\n9|`3aa14ff467e45931d4be7869df14a67cc6a50a042e51dcc1eb5721825ea82985` (equal to\n10|the CR record and to `git diff --binary` of the two OIDs). Every probe ran in\n11|isolated `git archive` copies of the exact candidate tree under\n12|`.temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/` (`cand/` probes, `cand-h/` shipped harness,\n13|`cand-m/` reviewer mutants, `cand-x/` tree-exact checks, `cand-fix/` the\n14|candidate-fix experiment); the live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD\n15|were never touched. Every instrument, raw log and subprocess exit is in\n16|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz` (paths below are relative to\n17|that archive). `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere; 0 `__pycache__` in any\n18|candidate copy.\n19|\n20|## Rework verification — the rev2 findings, graded on my own executed evidence\n21|\n22|Every rev2 probe (`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go`, 29 tests) was re-run\n23|unchanged against the new tree (`logs/10-rev2-probes-rerun.log`): 23 pass; the\n24|6 that fail are harness artifacts of the rev2 world (they installed a\n25|successor lease without publishing the checkpoint on the chain, expected\n26|`Status` to move to the superseded pair, asserted through a chain the\n27|landed reducer refuses, or were the rev2 harness fault already superseded) — each was re-driven with the rev3 fixtures in\n28|`probes/zz_review3_probe_test.go` (`logs/11-rev3-probes.log`). A finding is\n29|\"fixed\" only when the reported vector refuses AND a vector one step away\n30|behaves per the spec.\n31|\n32|| rev2 finding | Grade | Executed evidence |\n33|| --- | --- | --- |\n34|| P1-1 window / admission / journal keyed on the lease record's checkpoint (null for every epoch-1 owner) | **Fixed for the epoch-1 owner — the same root cause survives at a third site and in the new agreement rule → P1-1 below** | `TestR3EpochOneOwnerRestoreLaunchesAndRetryReattaches` (Run, real stores): lease `epoch=1 HasCheckpoint=false`, fold `has=true newest=C` → restore with a new operation **launches** with the op2 receipt, and an identical retry with different child facts **reattaches** to the one child. `TestR3UnpublishedCheckpointParksAtNewestArm`: chain newest C, caller C2 the chain never published → `parked(restore_policy)` at the \"not the newest published checkpoint\" arm, no binding installed. `TestR3UnnamedSourceJournalParks`: journal sourced from `sha256:d2d2…` → parked \"sourced from a superseded checkpoint\". The three re-pinned positives run with the chain carrying the checkpoint (`publishCheckpoint` appends idle + checkpointed stopped through `sessrepo.AppendEvent`; verified in the fixtures). Shipped narrowing rows N-window-fold, N-checkpoint-nullfold, N-materialization-nullfold, N-checkpoint-newest, N-checkpoint-agreement, N-materialization-agreement all KILLED ×2 (`logs/40`, `logs/41`). **But** the successor-lease half of the fix is wrong (P1-1 below): the strict agreement parks the ordinary post-takeover lifecycle, and `Run` still keys the profile closure on `Winner.Checkpoint`. |\n35|| P2-1 supersession destroyed the prior pair's receipt | **Fixed** | `TestR3SupersededPairIdenticalRetryReattaches` (Run): op2 and op3 each launch their own child post-window; an identical retry of op2 with different child facts **reattaches** to op2's child, the op2 receipt keeps its inode and mtime, `Status` keeps the first anchor, all three pairs replay through `Lookup`, exactly 3 receipts on disk. `TestR3SupersedeSamePairNoReplace`: a same-pair `Supersede` with different facts replays the recorded receipt (same inode, same bytes). `TestR3SupersedeRealKillSeams`: real SIGKILL after stage → no op2 receipt, anchor intact, the retry installs exactly one; real SIGKILL after install → the receipt is complete and the retry replays it. Reviewer mutant RV3-8 (pair commit rewritten as a replace-over rename) KILLED ×2 by `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays`. Residual: **P2-1 below** (the same-pair race through `Run` reports `launch`). |\n36|| P2-2 `Run` fell back to the session head when no checkpoint store was bound | **Fixed** | `TestR3NoCkptStoreIsUnknownNotNoClosure` on a chain that **folds** (the rev2 probe world did not): winner carries a checkpoint, `stores.Ckpt=nil` → `Run` errors with no decision; with the store → launch with the closure pair (`standard`, no source), never the head pair; an epoch-1 winner without a checkpoint still launches with no store on a checkpoint-free path (no over-refusal). RV3-7 (guard narrowed to restore mode) KILLED ×2 by `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails`. |\n37|| P3-1 losing-epoch arm of the `Emit` gate unpinned (RV7 survived twice) | **Fixed** | RV7 re-run KILLED ×2 by `TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses` (`logs/50`, `logs/51`). `TestN3EmitUnderLosingTupleRefusesAfterRunPark`: a losing presented `(1,A)` under the local winner `(2,S)` on a failed chain parks `stale_owner` and `Run` authors under `(2,S)`; a direct `Emit` under `(1,A)` refuses `stale_owner` at the mutation gate. |\n38|| P3-2 create-from-stopped through `Run` unpinned (RV11 survived twice) | **Fixed** | RV11 re-anchored to the new `if input.SessionBound { Supersede }` path, KILLED ×2 by `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow`. |\n39|| P3-3 denominator restated (41 vs 43) | **Partially fixed** | The table has 43 rows (`TestN3TraceabilityNamesExist`: rows=43, every named test exists). The producer publishes 43/43; I measure **39 of 43** (P3-3 below) — the four rows that touch the post-takeover lifecycle are pinned to a refusal the spec does not require. |\n40|| P3-4 foreground credential-requiring path bypassed the realm row | **Fixed** | `TestN2ProbeForegroundCredentialPathWithoutRealmRow` (re-run): foreground + `Smoke.Required` + cached passing smoke, no realm row → `refused capability_unavailable`. `TestN3ForegroundExpiredRealmRowTyped`: foreground + smoke required + expired realm row → typed `capability_unavailable`. RV3-5 (conditional narrowed back to background) KILLED ×2. |\n41|| P3-5 realm evidence order dependence | **Fixed** | `TestN2ProbeRealmEvidenceOrder` (re-run): both orders launch. `TestN3RealmThreeObjectsLastBinds`: two foreign objects then the binding one → launch. |\n42|| P3-6 expired / pre-reboot realm row refused with the reconcile class | **Fixed, with the bound stated** | `TestR2ProbeBackgroundCachedSmokeNeverAuthorizes` (re-run): expired row → `capability_unavailable`; pre-reboot row → `capability_unavailable`. `TestN3DeadRealmRowWithoutNeedKeepsBackendClass`: a caller that needs no realm row keeps `terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch` (the mapping does not widen). RV3-6 (mapping result ignored) KILLED ×2. Residual hygiene: P3-6 below (`realmRowUsable` restates the reconcile liveness predicate). |\n43|| P3-7 test hygiene | **Fixed** | `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission` exists and asserts what its name says; `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes` sources the journal from the published checkpoint and asserts `Lookup` for both pairs. |\n44|| P3-8 LOGBOOK reversal implicit | **Fixed** | The rev2 entry carries an explicit \"REVERSAL (P3-8, stated explicitly)\" paragraph; the rev3 entry is newest-first and additive (`git diff --numstat`: 28/0). |\n45|\n46|## What holds (verified myself, exact candidate tree)\n47|\n48|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n49|| --- | --- | --- |\n50|| gofmt / go vet / go build; GOOS=linux and GOOS=windows builds; GOOS=windows vet | all exit 0 | `logs/01-fmt-vet-build.log`, `logs/70-tree-exact-checks.log` |\n51|| tracecheck on the exact tree (registry untouched: contracts=64, sections=36, clauses 49/569) / `cataloggen -adopted … -check` | exit 0 / exit 0 | `logs/70` |\n52|| `go test ./internal/axpane -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 178 PASS lines, 0 FAIL | `logs/05-axpane-test-v.log` |\n53|| axpane + fencing + sessprofile + matjournal + sessckpt + provhost | all `ok` | `logs/71-six-packages.log` |\n54|| Shipped harness, isolated pristine copy, two full passes with raw per-plant output | 48/48 match both passes (47 KILLED + control SURVIVED); production blobs restored (OIDs equal to the candidate tree) | `logs/40`, `logs/41`, `logs/42-post-harness-blob-oids.log` |\n55|| Reviewer mutants (whole committed suite as killer, two passes) | 12 KILLED ×2 (RV7, RV11, RV3-1 agreement result ignored, RV3-2 steps 3/4 swapped, RV3-3 park reason collapsed, RV3-4 window check dropped, RV3-5, RV3-6, RV3-7, RV3-8, RV3-9 Lookup prefix, RV3-12 closure branch disabled); control SURVIVED ×2; RV3-10 (receipts-only scan) SURVIVED ×2 as the equivalence probe it was declared to be; **RV3-4b and RV3-11 SURVIVED ×2 with non-equivalent witnesses** (P3-1, P3-2 below) | `logs/50`, `logs/51`, `logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/*.log`, `logs/53-delta-witness-under-mutants.log` |\n56|| Real-kill after commit (`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`) + hooks + concurrency, ×2 | PASS ×2 | `logs/60-crash-rerun-x2.log` |\n57|| My real SIGKILL at both `Supersede` seams; identical-retry inode census on pair receipts; same-pair no-replace | as graded above | `TestR3SupersedeRealKillSeams`, `TestR3SupersededPairIdenticalRetryReattaches`, `TestR3SupersedeSamePairNoReplace` |\n58|| Decision-table plants (brief item 3) | remote interactive owner + stale journal → `attach_remote` (fencing precedes materialization); interactive remote owner + lapsed grant → `refused lease_conflict` (landed fencing order: grant expiry precedes direction; no token minted); journal one generation behind → `parked(restore_policy)`; head-only profile change outside the closure never becomes the launch profile; descriptor generation drift → `terminal_backend_stale_generation`; capability outside the closed §4.D set (`teleport`) → refused mismatch | `TestN3DecisionPlants/*` |\n59|| Composition bypass plants (brief item 2) | malformed winner holder equal to the local host → `invalid_arguments` (fencing grammar); no grant → refused; committed journal with an empty source → parked; the newest digest named with another checkpoint's bytes → parked at the identity arm; closure heads naming no chain event → `integrity_failure`; realm row with a null smoke result → refused (signature/shape); non-canonical entrypoint spelling → `local_precondition_failed`; in-window changed op through `Run` → `idempotency_mismatch` | `TestN3CompositionBypassPlants/*`; duplicated predicates: none beyond the fail-fast guards already justified in rev2 plus P3-6 below |\n60|| Cached sentinel / `managername` rule is structural | `Realm` carries `Caller`, `BrokerState`, `ServerGeneration`, `Remediation` only; 0 production identifiers named `sentinel`/`managername`/`AttestedServer`; a cached passing smoke record never authorizes (re-run probes) | `logs/80-hygiene.log` |\n61|| PID / process control / exec census | `pid`/`tmux` appear only in comments and the typed `TmuxServerGeneration` detail; no `os/exec`, no `syscall` in production; production imports are the landed owners plus stdlib | `logs/20-import-census.log` |\n62|| Changed paths / traceability / config / pycache / README+LOGBOOK | exactly the 23 candidate paths; `internal/traceability` untouched; `task-board.config.json` equal to base; 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the tree; README +62/−0, LOGBOOK +28/−0; README package section carries the test and harness commands and \"no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim\" | `logs/80` |\n63|| Race gate `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | **exit 0, `ok` in 333 s** (335 s wall) on a loaded host (load 7→12 while my harness passes overlapped its start; not idle). The CR construction's own configured 27-command suite was green (`coverage_unit=exact_command_shard required=27 green=27 failed=0`), and the producer's real race log shows sessquery `ok` in 496 s. Judgement: a host-capacity artifact under the old 10 m default, not a regression — the candidate cannot reach sessquery and sessquery cannot reach it; with the 25 m timeout the gate is green | `logs/30-sessquery-race.log`, `logs/20` (axpane↔sessquery deps 0/0 both directions incl. test deps; candidate touches 0 sessquery bytes) |\n64|\n65|## P1 — must fix before this leaf can be accepted\n66|\n67|### P1-1 The successor-lease half of the rev2 fix keys on the lease record's checkpoint in the wrong way: strict \"agreement\" parks the ordinary post-takeover lifecycle, and `Run` still derives the profile closure from the lease's handoff base (§5.3, §5.7, §13.10, §13.11 step 5, §2.4)\n68|\n69|A successor lease's `checkpoint_id` is the **handoff base** at takeover time and\n70|never moves: lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs and the\n71|landed `sessrepo` has no renewal API (`CreateLease`, `CompareAndSwapLease`,\n72|`GetLease`, `ListLeases`, `WinningLease` only — `logs/80`). Every checkpoint\n73|the successor owner publishes afterwards lands on the chain\n74|(`checkpoint.created`, checkpointed `session.stopped`, `session.resumed`)\n75|while the winning lease keeps naming C0. So \"the lease's checkpoint equals\n76|the fold's newest\" is true only until the new owner's first checkpoint.\n77|\n78|- `decide.go:687` `leaseCheckpointAgrees` requires\n79|  `Winner.Checkpoint == NewestCheckpointID` and is consulted by both\n80|  `checkMaterialization` and `admitCheckpoint`.\n81|  `TestN3PostTakeoverLifecycleRestoreLaunches` (`logs/11`), through `Run` on\n82|  real stores: epoch-1 owner stops with C0 (published), a LOCAL successor\n83|  lease `(2,S)` is minted through `CompareAndSwapLease` with base C0, the\n84|  successor owner appends `session.resumed`(C0) → `session.idle` →\n85|  checkpointed `session.stopped`(C1) — the landed reducer folds this chain\n86|  (`LoadNewestCheckpoint` → C1, no error). A restore on that owner with the\n87|  journal sourced from C1, checkpoint C1, presented `(2,S)` →\n88|  **`parked(restore_policy)` \"winning lease checkpoint disagrees with the\n89|  newest published checkpoint\"**. Same through `Decide`\n90|  (`TestN3PostTakeoverLifecycleDecide`). Every session that was ever taken\n91|  over and then continued can never restore on its owner again; the only\n92|  \"agreeing\" state is the instant after the handoff. The negatives stay\n93|  correct (`TestN3PostTakeoverStaleBaseParks`: naming the stale base C0 parks\n94|  at the journal/newest arms).\n95|- `run.go:213-216` loads the profile closure from\n96|  `observation.Winner.Checkpoint` whenever the winner carries one (even when\n97|  a different checkpoint is required), i.e. from the handoff base, not from\n98|  the checkpoint actually resumed. On the **exact tree** this is reachable\n99|  in launch mode (create from stopped, no checkpoint required):\n100|  `TestN3PostTakeoverLaunchModeProfileFromHandoffBase` (`logs/13`): the\n101|  successor owner changed the profile to `yolo` (authoritative, under\n102|  `(2,S)`) and stopped with C1 whose closure carries that change; the launch\n103|  carries **`standard`, no source** (C0's closure). The dangerous direction\n104|  `TestN3PostTakeoverLaunchModeYoloFromStaleBase` (`logs/14`): C0's closure\n105|  says `yolo`, the successor owner set the profile BACK to `standard` before\n106|  C1; the launch carries **`yolo` with mapping\n107|  `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`** on a session whose\n108|  authoritative profile is `standard`. In restore mode the same site is only\n109|  masked by the agreement park: with the agreement relaxed to \"a successor\n110|  lease implies a published newest\" (`cand-fix/`, the obvious candidate fix),\n111|  `TestFX_PostTakeoverProfileClosureSource` (`logs/12-fix-experiment.log`)\n112|  launches with `standard`/null instead of `yolo`/E. Fixing (a) alone\n113|  therefore turns a park into a wrong-profile launch.\n114|\n115|The rev2 brief's \"a successor lease's Checkpoint is the handoff base and\n116|must AGREE with the fold — assert that\" was my instruction, and as a strict\n117|equality it is wrong past the handoff instant; the producer implemented it\n118|literally. Required fix: the fold is the sole newest-checkpoint authority. The\n119|only fact a successor lease adds is the implication \"a checkpoint-carrying\n120|winner ⇒ the fold has a published newest\": assert it at ONE site every\n121|launch-class path passes (directly after the fencing arm, so it owns the\n122|decision for launch and restore alike, with or without a required\n123|checkpoint or journal) and park `restore_policy` when a checkpoint-carrying\n124|winner meets a null fold; assert nothing else about the lease's base\n125|(binding the base to a checkpoint the chain published is the takeover\n126|leaf's obligation — state it as a bound) and delete the equality. Derive the\n127|profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed: the required\n128|checkpoint when one is required; otherwise the fold's newest, loaded\n129|through `sessckpt` by that ID, when the fold has one; otherwise the session\n130|head (the epoch-1 bootstrap-retry path) — never `Winner.Checkpoint`. Re-pin: the\n131|post-takeover lifecycle positive (successor owner published C1 → restore\n132|launches with C1's closure profile, `Decide` and `Run`), the stale-base\n133|negative, the successor-with-null-fold negative, and the wrong-profile\n134|plants in both directions (`yolo`→`standard`, `standard`→`yolo`) through\n135|`Run`; ship a narrowing mutant on the null-fold conditional and one on the\n136|closure source (a mutant that reads `Winner.Checkpoint` again must die).\n137|Correct the README sentence (\"Resume derives the effective profile from the\n138|validated checkpoint's event-head closure\"), the rev3 LOGBOOK F1 (\"a\n139|successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\") and TRACEABILITY\n140|accordingly.\n141|\n142|## P2 — fix in the same rework\n143|\n144|### P2-1 Post-window same-pair race through `Run` reports `launch` with the winner's child (§4.1, §4.C create/restore rows)\n145|`Store.Supersede` replays the winner's receipt on the link `EEXIST` but\n146|returns no replay signal, and `run.go:284-289` reports the decision unchanged.\n147|`TestN3PostWindowSamePairRaceThroughRun` (`logs/15`): post-window, a\n148|concurrent wrapper records the same new pair between stage and link (played\n149|through `Hooks.AfterStage`); the loser's outcome is **`launch`** with\n150|`Binding.TerminalInstanceID = 3333` (the winner's child) while its admitted\n151|descriptor names its own instance `2222`. The in-window `Bind` path flips\n152|the same race to `reattach` (`TestRunConcurrentLaunchReattaches`); the\n153|post-window path does not. §4.1: an identical retry \"returns or reattaches\n154|to the one recorded wrapper/child\". Make `Supersede` report replay (or\n155|compare the returned instance with the candidate) and flip the outcome to\n156|`ActionReattach` with the recorded receipt; pin it through `Run` with the\n157|hook and ship a narrowing mutant (a replay that keeps `launch`).\n158|\n159|## P3\n160|\n161|- **P3-1** Unpinned widening: the window closing on the LEASE record's\n162|  checkpoint while the fold names none. RV3-4b\n163|  (`return input.HasNewestCheckpoint || (HasWinner && Winner.HasCheckpoint)`)\n164|  SURVIVED the whole suite twice; witness `TestDX_WindowLeaseCheckpointNullFold`\n165|  (`logs/53`): pristine → `refused idempotency_mismatch`; under the mutant →\n166|  **launch** for an in-window changed op on a bound session with a successor\n167|  lease carrying an unpublished checkpoint. Add that negative and a harness\n168|  row.\n169|- **P3-2** Unpinned absence-vs-failure arm: `Run` swallowing the fold error.\n170|  RV3-11 (`LoadNewestCheckpoint` error → `has=false`) SURVIVED twice; witness\n171|  `TestDX_UnfolderableChainThroughRun`: pristine → error, no decision; under\n172|  the mutant → **launch** over a chain the landed reducer refuses\n173|  (`profile.changed` under a successor lease while `creating`). Add a `Run`\n174|  test with an unfolderable chain and a harness row.\n175|- **P3-3** Ratio: the table has 43 rows and every named test exists, but 43/43\n176|  is not the honest number. Measured: **39 of 43** — \"Materialization\n177|  validity gates local resume\", \"Checkpoint admission gates resume\",\n178|  \"After-restore sequence 1-5\" pin the agreement park the spec does not\n179|  require, and \"Effective profile derived with source\" is driven only for\n180|  the epoch-1 owner (P1-1). Re-derive after the rework and name the gaps if\n181|  any remain.\n182|- **P3-4** Outcome evidence hygiene: the results table and\n183|  `rev3-evidence.tar.gz` describe a \"27-command validation suite\" that is\n184|  not the configured `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`.\n185|  `cmd06`–`cmd27` in the archive are ad-hoc `-run` masks that matched no test\n186|  (\"no tests to run\" ×20), `go test ./internal/doctor/` for a package that\n187|  does not exist (reported as \"PRE-EXISTING\" failure) and \"bundle scripts\n188|  skipped-dirty\" — none of these are configured commands (spawn log\n189|  `RUN-260917-4c75bd` exec-87/93). `cmd01`, `cmd02` and `cmd05` are real\n190|  (38 packages; race `ok` incl. sessquery 495 s). The authoritative gate is\n191|  the CR construction's own run of the configured suite\n192|  (`coverage_unit=exact_command_shard required=27 green=27 failed=0`), which\n193|  is green. Describe that, not a fabricated list.\n194|- **P3-5** The outcome `TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix-rev3.md` names\n195|  two tests that exist nowhere in the tree (`TestTerminalBackendRefusesUnproven`,\n196|  `TestV4TerminalPayloadsParse`; `logs/81`, `logs/82`); the in-tree\n197|  TRACEABILITY.md and `TestConformanceMatrixCompleteness` are consistent.\n198|- **P3-6** `realmRowUsable` (`decide.go:958`) restates the reconcile liveness\n199|  and generation predicate (`observed_at ≤ now < expires_at`, generation\n200|  digest equality) to classify the refusal; classification-only and\n201|  fail-closed in both directions, but it is a second copy of a landed rule.\n202|  Derive the class from the reconcile error or state the copy as a bound.\n203|- **P3-7** The Provider Identity Record is not bound to SESSION_ID: an\n204|  identity minted for another session with the same provider/version\n205|  launches (`TestN3CompositionBypassPlants/identity_record_for_another_session`).\n206|  The landed `VerifyIdentityBuild` checks provider and version only; either\n207|  bind the record's `session_id` in the wrapper (as the checkpoint arm does)\n208|  or state the bound that the caller loads the identity from the session's\n209|  own store.\n210|- **P3-8** Prose that P1-1 makes false: README \"Resume derives the effective\n211|  profile from the validated checkpoint's event-head closure\"; LOGBOOK rev3\n212|  F1 \"a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\";\n213|  TRACEABILITY rows citing \"with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing\".\n214|  Fix with the rework.\n215|\n216|## Coverage statement\n217|\n218|Producer claim: 43 of 43 AC rows driven. Table rows: 43 (counted). Honest\n219|ratio: **39 of 43** (P3-3). The rev2 findings are fixed on the epoch-1\n220|owner; the same root cause (keying on the lease record's checkpoint) now\n221|reaches the successor owner through the agreement rule and the profile\n222|closure source, both executed above.\n223|\n224|## Instruments (all in the evidence archive)\n225|\n226|`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go` (rev2 probes re-run unchanged),\n227|`probes/zz_review3_probe_test.go` (21 probes: R3 rework re-drives, N3 new\n228|plants, decision-table and composition plants, the race, the traceability\n229|census), `probes/zz_review3_delta_test.go` (delta witnesses),\n230|`probes/zz_review3_fixexp_test.go` (candidate-fix experiment, `cand-fix/`\n231|only), `review3_mutants.py` (16 rows, whole-suite killer), `logs/01`, `05`,\n232|`10`–`15` (probe runs), `20` (import census), `30` (race gate), `40`–`42`\n233|(shipped harness ×2 + blob OIDs), `50`–`53` (reviewer mutants ×2 + delta\n234|witnesses), `60` (crash reruns), `70`–`71` (tree-exact checks, six\n235|packages), `80`–`82` (hygiene, name censuses), `REVIEW-MANIFEST.txt`.\n236|\n237|Verdict recorded by RUN-260917-19551c; no product edits, commits, checkpoints\n238|or integration were performed; the isolated copies are deleted after\n239|attachment.","final_result":true}}}
