{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":340,"recorded_at":1780531400000675,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b196-3a18-7da2-8891-6bcc08e971e8"},"task_id":"01a0b196-3a18-7da2-8891-6bcc08e971e8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b196-3a18-7da2-8891-6bcc08e971e8","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/run.go`.\n1|package axpane\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/config\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// Request is the complete Run surface: the session and bootstrap\n14|// operation under decision plus every modeled-caller fact the\n15|// adapters cannot load from the durable stores (sync state,\n16|// provider build and identity, backend documents, realm readiness,\n17|// presentation geometry). The stores supply configuration,\n18|// sessions, leases, journals, checkpoints, and bindings.\n19|type Request struct {\n20|\tSessionID            string\n21|\tBootstrapOperationID string\n22|\tMode                 Mode\n23|\n24|\tConfigInputs    config.Inputs\n25|\tConfigOverrides config.Overrides\n26|\n27|\t// Presented is the local fencing token; Observe carries the\n28|\t// caller-reported sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts.\n29|\tPresented fencing.PresentedToken\n30|\tObserve   fencing.ObserveInput\n31|\n32|\t// Materialization selects the required journal: when Required\n33|\t// is set the adapter loads ID and the decision requires the\n34|\t// committed phase (after-restore step 3).\n35|\tMaterializationID       string\n36|\tMaterializationRequired bool\n37|\n38|\t// Checkpoint selects the resume checkpoint: when Required is\n39|\t// set the adapter loads ID and the decision admits it.\n40|\tCheckpointID       string\n41|\tCheckpointRequired bool\n42|\n43|\tProvider ProviderFacts\n44|\tSmoke    SmokeFacts\n45|\tRealm    Realm\n46|\tBackend  BackendFacts\n47|\n48|\t// Entrypoint is the wrapper argv.\n49|\tEntrypoint []string\n50|\n51|\t// HostBinding is the AX-validated host-local binding subset\n52|\t// the supplied descriptor must match. Geometry and\n53|\t// interactivity shape the supplied descriptor; InstanceID\n54|\t// pins the terminal instance, or mints a fresh UUIDv7 when\n55|\t// empty.\n56|\tHostBinding terminalbackend.InstanceBinding\n57|\tInteractive bool\n58|\tColumns     uint16\n59|\tRows        uint16\n60|\tInstanceID  string\n61|\n62|\t// RemoteInteractive reports that the remote owner holds the\n63|\t// session in an interactive terminal (after-restore step 4).\n64|\tRemoteInteractive bool\n65|\n66|\t// LocalHostID authors parked events; CreatedAt stamps them.\n67|\tLocalHostID string\n68|\tCreatedAt   string\n69|\n70|\t// Hooks arms the bootstrap binding crash boundaries.\n71|\tHooks *Hooks\n72|}\n73|\n74|// Outcome is the one Run result: the decision plus the durable\n75|// effects it authorized. Exactly one effect applies: a launch binds\n76|// the bootstrap pair (superseding after the window closed), a\n77|// reattach returns the recorded binding, a parked or remote-offer\n78|// decision with a locally held, verified winner and a foldable\n79|// lifecycle authors the parked event, and every other outcome\n80|// writes nothing.\n81|type Outcome struct {\n82|\tDecision Decision\n83|\t// Binding is the bound receipt on launch and the recorded\n84|\t// receipt on reattach, nil otherwise.\n85|\tBinding *Binding\n86|\t// Event is the authored parked event reference and bytes;\n87|\t// Emitted is false when the decision parks without a locally\n88|\t// held winner, without a foldable lifecycle, or when the\n89|\t// outcome is neither parked nor a remote offer. A park without\n90|\t// chain authority parks without evidence, never by manufacturing\n91|\t// a sequence collision under another host's lease.\n92|\tEvent     *sessrepo.EventRef\n93|\tEventJSON []byte\n94|\tEmitted   bool\n95|}\n96|\n97|// Run orchestrates the wrapper: validate configuration, load the\n98|// logical session, derive the fold's newest checkpoint, prove the\n99|// bootstrap binding state, observe the winning lease, load\n100|// materialization, checkpoint, and profile state, decide through\n101|// the pure core, then apply exactly the authorized durable\n102|// effect. A store failure propagates as an error with no decision:\n103|// unknown is never absence and never a launch.\n104|func Run(stores Stores, request Request) (Outcome, error) {\n105|\tempty := Outcome{}\n106|\tif stores.Repo == nil || stores.Pane == nil {\n107|\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run carries no repository or binding store\")\n108|\t}\n109|\t// The request hooks arm a copy of the binding handle: Run never\n110|\t// mutates the caller's store.\n111|\tpane := *stores.Pane\n112|\tpaneStore := pane.WithHooks(request.Hooks)\n113|\tinput := Input{\n114|\t\tSessionID:               request.SessionID,\n115|\t\tBootstrapOperationID:    request.BootstrapOperationID,\n116|\t\tMode:                    request.Mode,\n117|\t\tPresented:               request.Presented,\n118|\t\tProvider:                request.Provider,\n119|\t\tSmoke:                   request.Smoke,\n120|\t\tRealm:                   request.Realm,\n121|\t\tBackend:                 request.Backend,\n122|\t\tEntrypoint:              request.Entrypoint,\n123|\t\tHostBinding:             request.HostBinding,\n124|\t\tRemoteInteractive:       request.RemoteInteractive,\n125|\t\tInteractive:             request.Interactive,\n126|\t\tCheckpointRequired:      request.CheckpointRequired,\n127|\t\tCheckpointID:            request.CheckpointID,\n128|\t\tMaterializationRequired: request.MaterializationRequired,\n129|\t}\n130|\tinput.ConfigErr = ValidateConfig(request.ConfigInputs, request.ConfigOverrides)\n131|\n132|\tknown, _, err := LoadSession(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n133|\tif err != nil {\n134|\t\treturn empty, err\n135|\t}\n136|\tinput.SessionKnown = known\n137|\n138|\tpair, pairFound, err := paneStore.Lookup(request.SessionID, request.BootstrapOperationID)\n139|\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\treturn empty, err\n141|\t}\n142|\tif pairFound {\n143|\t\tduplicate := pair\n144|\t\tinput.ExistingBinding = &duplicate\n145|\t}\n146|\tbound, err := paneStore.SessionBound(request.SessionID)\n147|\tif err != nil {\n148|\t\treturn empty, err\n149|\t}\n150|\tinput.SessionBound = bound\n151|\n152|\tif known {\n153|\t\thas, newest, err := LoadNewestCheckpoint(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n154|\t\tif err != nil {\n155|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n156|\t\t}\n157|\t\tinput.HasNewestCheckpoint = has\n158|\t\tinput.NewestCheckpointID = newest\n159|\t}\n160|\n161|\tvar observation fencing.Observation\n162|\tif known {\n163|\t\tobserved, err := ObserveOwnership(stores.Repo, request.SessionID, request.Observe)\n164|\t\tif err != nil {\n165|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n166|\t\t}\n167|\t\tobservation = observed\n168|\t}\n169|\tinput.Observation = observation\n170|\n171|\t// The winner's checkpoint closure drives the resume profile,\n172|\t// so a winner that carries a checkpoint with no checkpoint\n173|\t// store bound is unknown, not \"no closure\": deriving from\n174|\t// the session head instead would silently promote a\n175|\t// head-only change to the launch profile. Fail the run.\n176|\tif known && observation.HasWinner && observation.Winner.HasCheckpoint && stores.Ckpt == nil {\n177|\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run requires the winner checkpoint closure with no checkpoint store\")\n178|\t}\n179|\n180|\tif request.MaterializationRequired {\n181|\t\tif stores.Mat == nil {\n182|\t\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run requires a materialization with no journal store\")\n183|\t\t}\n184|\t\tjournal, admitted, err := LoadMaterialization(stores.Mat, request.MaterializationID)\n185|\t\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\tinput.Journal = journal\n189|\t\tinput.JournalOK = admitted\n190|\t}\n191|\tif request.CheckpointRequired {\n192|\t\tif stores.Ckpt == nil {\n193|\t\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run requires a checkpoint with no checkpoint store\")\n194|\t\t}\n195|\t\tdoc, err := LoadCheckpoint(stores.Ckpt, request.CheckpointID)\n196|\t\tif err != nil {\n197|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n198|\t\t}\n199|\t\tinput.CheckpointDoc = doc\n200|\t}\n201|\tif known {\n202|\t\trecord, events, err := LoadProfile(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n203|\t\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n205|\t\t}\n206|\t\tinput.ProfileRecord = record\n207|\t\tinput.ProfileEvents = events\n208|\t\t// Resume derives the effective profile from the validated\n209|\t\t// checkpoint's event-head closure, never the session head,\n210|\t\t// so a head-only or losing-lease change cannot become the\n211|\t\t// launch profile (§13.10, §2.4). The heads come from the\n212|\t\t// winner's own checkpoint when the winner carries one.\n213|\t\tif observation.HasWinner && observation.Winner.HasCheckpoint && stores.Ckpt != nil {\n214|\t\t\tdoc := input.CheckpointDoc\n215|\t\t\tif !request.CheckpointRequired || request.CheckpointID != observation.Winner.Checkpoint {\n216|\t\t\t\tloaded, err := LoadCheckpoint(stores.Ckpt, observation.Winner.Checkpoint)\n217|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n218|\t\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n219|\t\t\t\t}\n220|\t\t\t\tdoc = loaded\n221|\t\t\t}\n222|\t\t\tif len(doc) > 0 {\n223|\t\t\t\theads, err := checkpointHeads(doc)\n224|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n225|\t\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n226|\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\tinput.ProfileHeads = heads\n228|\t\t\t}\n229|\t\t} else if request.CheckpointRequired && len(input.CheckpointDoc) > 0 {\n230|\t\t\theads, err := checkpointHeads(input.CheckpointDoc)\n231|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n232|\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n233|\t\t\t}\n234|\t\t\tinput.ProfileHeads = heads\n235|\t\t}\n236|\t}\n237|\n238|\tinstance := request.InstanceID\n239|\tif instance == \"\" {\n240|\t\tminted, err := MintInstanceIDRandom()\n241|\t\tif err != nil {\n242|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n243|\t\t}\n244|\t\tinstance = minted\n245|\t}\n246|\tdescriptorDoc, err := BuildDescriptor(DescriptorParams{\n247|\t\tBinding: BindingRef{\n248|\t\t\tBindingDigest:         request.HostBinding.TerminalBindingID,\n249|\t\t\tBackendID:             request.HostBinding.BackendID,\n250|\t\t\tImplementationVersion: request.HostBinding.ImplementationVersion,\n251|\t\t\tProtocolVersion:       request.HostBinding.ProtocolVersion,\n252|\t\t\tGeneration:            request.HostBinding.Generation,\n253|\t\t},\n254|\t\tInstanceID:  instance,\n255|\t\tInteractive: request.Interactive,\n256|\t\tColumns:     request.Columns,\n257|\t\tRows:        request.Rows,\n258|\t})\n259|\tif err != nil {\n260|\t\treturn empty, err\n261|\t}\n262|\tinput.Descriptor = descriptorDoc\n263|\n264|\tdecision := Decide(input)\n265|\toutcome := Outcome{Decision: decision}\n266|\tswitch decision.Action {\n267|\tcase ActionLaunch:\n268|\t\tcandidate := Binding{\n269|\t\t\tSessionID:          request.SessionID,\n270|\t\t\tOperationID:        request.BootstrapOperationID,\n271|\t\t\tTerminalInstanceID: instance,\n272|\t\t}\n273|\t\tcandidate.BindingDigest = BindingDigest(candidate)\n274|\t\t// A launch reaches here only for an unrecorded pair (a\n275|\t\t// recorded pair reattaches instead). On a bound session\n276|\t\t// the decision already applied the window predicate, so\n277|\t\t// a launch here is post-window and records its own pair\n278|\t\t// receipt through Supersede, keeping every superseded\n279|\t\t// receipt; on an unbound session the launch binds\n280|\t\t// no-replace. A mismatch from Bind is a concurrent\n281|\t\t// changed-operation commit the retry observes through\n282|\t\t// Lookup.\n283|\t\tif input.SessionBound {\n284|\t\t\tbound, err := paneStore.Supersede(request.SessionID, request.BootstrapOperationID, candidate)\n285|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n286|\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n287|\t\t\t}\n288|\t\t\tduplicate := bound\n289|\t\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n290|\t\t\tbreak\n291|\t\t}\n292|\t\tbound, reattached, err := paneStore.Bind(request.SessionID, request.BootstrapOperationID, candidate)\n293|\t\tif err != nil {\n294|\t\t\t// A concurrent changed-operation commit surfaces\n295|\t\t\t// here as idempotency_mismatch: the caller's retry\n296|\t\t\t// observes the winner through Status and decides\n297|\t\t\t// the refused outcome.\n298|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n299|\t\t}\n300|\t\tif reattached {\n301|\t\t\t// A concurrent wrapper won the bind between Status\n302|\t\t\t// and Bind: the pair is bound, so this run\n303|\t\t\t// reattaches to the recorded child instead of\n304|\t\t\t// launching a second one.\n305|\t\t\toutcome.Decision.Action = ActionReattach\n306|\t\t\toutcome.Decision.Detail = \"reattach to the one recorded wrapper/child\"\n307|\t\t}\n308|\t\tduplicate := bound\n309|\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n310|\tcase ActionReattach:\n311|\t\tduplicate := *input.ExistingBinding\n312|\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n313|\tcase ActionParked, ActionAttachRemote, ActionTakeoverOffer:\n314|\t\tif !observation.HasWinner {\n315|\t\t\t// No winner establishes no authority: session.parked\n316|\t\t\t// requires a winning lease ID, so the decision\n317|\t\t\t// parks without authoring an event.\n318|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n319|\t\t}\n320|\t\tif observation.Winner.HolderHostID != observation.LocalHostID {\n321|\t\t\t// A remote winner holds the lease: the local\n322|\t\t\t// wrapper parks without manufacturing a sequence\n323|\t\t\t// collision under another host's lease (§5.2: the\n324|\t\t\t// winning owner serializes state-changing\n325|\t\t\t// events). No host-local chain record exists for\n326|\t\t\t// a remote park; the decision itself is the\n327|\t\t\t// parked evidence.\n328|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n329|\t\t}\n330|\t\tfoldable, err := canAuthorParked(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n331|\t\tif err != nil {\n332|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n333|\t\t}\n334|\t\tif !foldable {\n335|\t\t\t// The §5.7 table cannot fold session.parked from\n336|\t\t\t// the derived state: the decision parks without\n337|\t\t\t// authoring an unfolderable lifecycle event.\n338|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n339|\t\t}\n340|\t\treference, raw, err := emitParked(stores.Repo, decision, observation, request)\n341|\t\tif err != nil {\n342|\t\t\t// The mutation gate refused (unverified,\n343|\t\t\t// ambiguous, failed handoff, lapsed grant): the\n344|\t\t\t// decision parks without chain evidence rather\n345|\t\t\t// than failing the run. A store failure also\n346|\t\t\t// lands here; unknown is never a launch, but the\n347|\t\t\t// parked decision stands with no event.\n348|\t\t\t// Emit-level refusals are distinguished by the\n349|\t\t\t// fencing owner; repository failures propagate.\n350|\t\t\tif fencing.IsParked(err) || isFencingRefusal(err) {\n351|\t\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n352|\t\t\t}\n353|\t\t\toutcome.Emitted = false\n354|\t\t\treturn outcome, err\n355|\t\t}\n356|\t\toutcome.Event = &reference\n357|\t\toutcome.EventJSON = raw\n358|\t\toutcome.Emitted = true\n359|\t}\n360|\treturn outcome, nil\n361|}\n362|\n363|// isFencingRefusal reports whether err is a fencing gate refusal\n364|// (as opposed to a repository failure): the parked decision stands\n365|// with no chain evidence when the mutation gate refuses.\n366|func isFencingRefusal(err error) bool {\n367|\tif err == nil {\n368|\t\treturn false\n369|\t}\n370|\tif fencing.IsParked(err) {\n371|\t\treturn true\n372|\t}\n373|\treturn errors.Is(err, fencing.ErrInvalidArguments) ||\n374|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrLeaseConflict) ||\n375|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrNotOwner) ||\n376|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrStaleOwner)\n377|}\n378|\n379|// emitParked authors the parked event under the winning lease the\n380|// local host holds, with the current chain linkage: the next\n381|// sequence under the winning lease, or sequence 1 referencing the\n382|// predecessor head when the winner succeeded the tail lease. The\n383|// presented token is the winning tuple itself, so the mutation\n384|// gate authorizes the locally held winner; the decision's stale or\n385|// unverified presented token never authors.\n386|func emitParked(repository *sessrepo.Repository, decision Decision, observation fencing.Observation, request Request) (sessrepo.EventRef, []byte, error) {\n387|\trecordID, tail, err := ChainTail(repository, request.SessionID)\n388|\tif err != nil {\n389|\t\treturn sessrepo.EventRef{}, nil, err\n390|\t}\n391|\tvar sequence uint64 = 1\n392|\tpredecessors := []string{recordID}\n393|\tif tail != nil {\n394|\t\tif tail.LeaseID == observation.Winner.LeaseID {\n395|\t\t\tsequence = tail.LeaseSequence + 1\n396|\t\t}\n397|\t\tpredecessors = []string{tail.EventID}\n398|\t}\n399|\tpresented := fencing.PresentedToken{\n400|\t\tSessionID: request.SessionID,\n401|\t\tEpoch:     observation.Winner.Epoch,\n402|\t\tLeaseID:   observation.Winner.LeaseID,\n403|\t}\n404|\treturn EmitParked(repository, decision, EmitParams{\n405|\t\tSessionID:     request.SessionID,\n406|\t\tCreatedByHost: request.LocalHostID,\n407|\t\tLeaseEpoch:    observation.Winner.Epoch,\n408|\t\tLeaseID:       observation.Winner.LeaseID,\n409|\t\tLeaseSequence: sequence,\n410|\t\tPredecessors:  predecessors,\n411|\t\tCreatedAt:     request.CreatedAt,\n412|\t\tPresented:     presented,\n413|\t\tObservation:   observation,\n414|\t})\n415|}","final_result":true}}}
