{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":342,"recorded_at":1780531400000679,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b196-39da-7fb3-83e7-3eafe0f429f6"},"task_id":"01a0b196-39da-7fb3-83e7-3eafe0f429f6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b196-39da-7fb3-83e7-3eafe0f429f6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/decide.go`.\n1|package axpane\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"errors\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"time\"\n8|\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/matjournal\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/resumesmoke\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessprofile\"\n17|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n18|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n19|)\n20|\n21|// Action is exactly one wrapper outcome. Decide returns one and only\n22|// one; there is no combined or fallback outcome.\n23|type Action string\n24|\n25|const (\n26|\t// ActionLaunch starts the provider under the winning lease with\n27|\t// the validated descriptor and fencing token.\n28|\tActionLaunch Action = \"launch\"\n29|\t// ActionReattach reattaches to the one recorded wrapper/child\n30|\t// after a lost result: the bootstrap pair matches the durable\n31|\t// binding and every gate passes again.\n32|\tActionReattach Action = \"reattach\"\n33|\t// ActionAttachRemote offers remote attach: another host owns the\n34|\t// session in an interactive terminal and the attach capability\n35|\t// is admitted. It authorizes no lease mutation.\n36|\tActionAttachRemote Action = \"attach_remote\"\n37|\t// ActionTakeoverOffer offers takeover: another host owns the\n38|\t// session in an interactive terminal but remote attach is not\n39|\t// available (attach capability unproven). It starts no runtime.\n40|\t// A remote owner outside an interactive terminal parks instead\n41|\t// (§4.2 step 5: parked in all other cases).\n42|\tActionTakeoverOffer Action = \"takeover_offer\"\n43|\t// ActionParked parks without launching the provider, carrying\n44|\t// the Section 5.2 session.parked reason vocabulary.\n45|\tActionParked Action = \"parked\"\n46|\t// ActionRefused refuses: a static validation failed and there is\n47|\t// no parked direction that a state change could resolve.\n48|\tActionRefused Action = \"refused\"\n49|)\n50|\n51|// Refusal classes are the Section 15 codes the wrapper surfaces.\n52|// Landed-gate codes pass through verbatim; the wrapper mints no code.\n53|const (\n54|\t// ClassInvalidConfig reports a configuration that fails\n55|\t// validation (config.Load through ValidateConfig).\n56|\tClassInvalidConfig = \"invalid_config\"\n57|\t// ClassInvalidArguments reports a malformed wrapper call: an\n58|\t// unknown SESSION_ID, an unknown caller kind or mode, or a\n59|\t// malformed presented fencing token.\n60|\tClassInvalidArguments = \"invalid_arguments\"\n61|\t// ClassIntegrityFailure reports profile derivation input the\n62|\t// reducer refuses: the chain cannot be trusted.\n63|\tClassIntegrityFailure = \"integrity_failure\"\n64|\t// ClassProfileMappingUnavailable is the Section 2.4 resume\n65|\t// failure: the adapter cannot map the stored profile for the\n66|\t// probed provider version.\n67|\tClassProfileMappingUnavailable = \"profile_mapping_unavailable\"\n68|)\n69|\n70|// Mode selects the wrapper path: a fresh activation (the Section 4.C\n71|// create row) or the after-restore first start (the restore row). It\n72|// selects both the fencing entry and the backend capability the\n73|// admitted set must confer.\n74|type Mode string\n75|\n76|const (\n77|\t// ModeLaunch gates through fencing AuthorizeActivation and the\n78|\t// create capability dependencies.\n79|\tModeLaunch Mode = \"launch\"\n80|\t// ModeRestore gates through fencing AuthorizeRestore and the\n81|\t// restore capability dependencies.\n82|\tModeRestore Mode = \"restore\"\n83|)\n84|\n85|// Caller kinds are the closed §4.2 realm vocabulary.\n86|const (\n87|\t// CallerForeground is an interactive operator-side caller.\n88|\tCallerForeground = \"foreground\"\n89|\t// CallerBackground is a background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n90|\t// or restore worker: it must never create a\n91|\t// credential-dependent tmux server.\n92|\tCallerBackground = \"background\"\n93|)\n94|\n95|// Realm carries the §4.2 caller realm and broker readiness the\n96|// credential-conditional arm decides over. There is deliberately no\n97|// member for a cached sentinel result, a managername observation,\n98|// or any attested-server boolean: none authorizes resume, so none\n99|// is an input. A background caller, and any caller on a path that\n100|// requires provider credentials, authorizes only through the\n101|// admitted credential_capable_execution_realm Capability Evidence\n102|// row bound to the exact host binding, probed provider build, and\n103|// current generation (§4.C conditional rows, §4.2, §4.D); the bare\n104|// boolean previously carried here never authorizes and is removed.\n105|type Realm struct {\n106|\t// Caller is CallerForeground or CallerBackground.\n107|\tCaller string\n108|\t// BrokerState, ServerGeneration, and Remediation are the typed\n109|\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n110|\t// carries. They are required: an empty member refuses\n111|\t// invalid_arguments instead of emitting an untyped refusal.\n112|\t// ServerGeneration must equal the current AX-known raw\n113|\t// generation the backend admission binds to; a stale generation\n114|\t// refuses capability_unavailable, never launches.\n115|\tBrokerState      string\n116|\tServerGeneration string\n117|\tRemediation      string\n118|}\n119|\n120|// Closed capability names the wrapper's conditional arms evaluate.\n121|// They repeat the §4.D registry rows the backend admission proves;\n122|// the wrapper invents no capability.\n123|const (\n124|\t// credentialRealmCapability is the §4.D row a background caller\n125|\t// must hold: the exact-instance sentinel plus provider-auth\n126|\t// smoke bound to the terminal binding, provider build,\n127|\t// generation digest, OS version, and expiry.\n128|\tcredentialRealmCapability = \"credential_capable_execution_realm\"\n129|\t// headlessCreationCapability is the §4.C create-row conditional\n130|\t// a non-interactive create must hold.\n131|\theadlessCreationCapability = \"headless_creation\"\n132|)\n133|\n134|// ProviderFacts carries the probed provider build, the stored\n135|// identity, and the optional discovery proof the provider-identity\n136|// arm decides over.\n137|type ProviderFacts struct {\n138|\t// Build is the exact probed build tuple.\n139|\tBuild provhost.BuildTuple\n140|\t// Identity is the stored Provider Identity Record document.\n141|\tIdentity []byte\n142|\t// Discovery is the NativeDiscoveryProof document, meaningful\n143|\t// only when HasDiscovery is set.\n144|\tDiscovery    []byte\n145|\tHasDiscovery bool\n146|\t// DiscoveryContext binds the proof to host-side facts.\n147|\tDiscoveryContext provhost.DiscoveryContext\n148|}\n149|\n150|// SmokeFacts carries the provider-auth smoke precondition: the\n151|// stored smoke record plus the typed target-auth details the\n152|// target_auth_missing refusal carries when the smoke is required\n153|// and fails.\n154|type SmokeFacts struct {\n155|\t// Required reports that provider credentials are required, so\n156|\t// the smoke must pass (the §4.C create/restore rows).\n157|\tRequired bool\n158|\t// Record is the stored smoke record document.\n159|\tRecord []byte\n160|\t// Target carries the typed provider/build/version/generation\n161|\t// details. Every member is required when the smoke is\n162|\t// required: an empty member refuses invalid_arguments instead\n163|\t// of emitting an untyped refusal.\n164|\tTarget axerror.TargetAuth\n165|\t// MacOSVersion is recorded here because TargetAuth carries it;\n166|\t// it is the version the smoke evidence binds, not a fresh\n167|\t// observation.\n168|}\n169|\n170|// BackendFacts carries the backend identity documents the §4.B arm\n171|// decides over.\n172|type BackendFacts struct {\n173|\t// Manifest, Probe, and Evidence are the raw documents parsed by\n174|\t// the terminalbackend owner.\n175|\tManifest []byte\n176|\tProbe    []byte\n177|\tEvidence [][]byte\n178|\t// RawGeneration is the AX-known raw generation the admission\n179|\t// binds to; Verify checks evidence signatures.\n180|\tRawGeneration string\n181|\tVerify        terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier\n182|\t// Now is the admission instant for evidence liveness.\n183|\tNow time.Time\n184|}\n185|\n186|// Input is the complete Decide surface: validated configuration,\n187|// the loaded session, the local lease view, materialization and\n188|// checkpoint state, the profile chain, provider identity, backend\n189|// identity, realm readiness, and the bootstrap binding. I/O-free\n190|// callers build it by hand; Run builds it through the gates.go\n191|// adapters over the durable stores.\n192|type Input struct {\n193|\t// SessionID is the logical session under decision.\n194|\tSessionID string\n195|\t// BootstrapOperationID is the caller-stable bootstrap operation.\n196|\tBootstrapOperationID string\n197|\t// Mode selects the fencing entry and capability row.\n198|\tMode Mode\n199|\n200|\t// ConfigErr is the ValidateConfig outcome; non-nil refuses\n201|\t// invalid_config.\n202|\tConfigErr error\n203|\t// SessionKnown reports that the logical session loaded; false\n204|\t// refuses invalid_arguments.\n205|\tSessionKnown bool\n206|\n207|\t// ExistingBinding is the proven bootstrap receipt for THIS\n208|\t// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) pair, or nil when the\n209|\t// pair is unrecorded. A recorded pair reattaches; an\n210|\t// unrecorded pair on a bound session inside the bootstrap\n211|\t// window refuses idempotency_mismatch; an unrecorded pair\n212|\t// after the window closed installs a new receipt and\n213|\t// launches. Superseded pairs keep their receipts, so an\n214|\t// identical retry of any recorded pair replays its own\n215|\t// receipt even after later pairs superseded it.\n216|\tExistingBinding *Binding\n217|\t// SessionBound reports that the session has any recorded\n218|\t// binding (the first-binding anchor or any pair receipt).\n219|\t// Together with the window predicate it drives the\n220|\t// changed-operation arm: an unrecorded pair on a bound\n221|\t// session inside the window refuses idempotency_mismatch,\n222|\t// while an unbound session binds fresh.\n223|\tSessionBound bool\n224|\t// HasNewestCheckpoint and NewestCheckpointID carry the\n225|\t// landed chain fold's newest checkpoint (sessstate.Reduce\n226|\t// over the authoritative chain: Projection.HasCheckpoint\n227|\t// and Newest.ID from checkpoint.created, checkpointed\n228|\t// session.stopped, and session.resumed). This is the\n229|\t// authoritative \"newest checkpoint\" (§5.7\n230|\t// newest_checkpoint_id, §14.4): the window predicate,\n231|\t// checkpoint admission, and journal source binding all read\n232|\t// this fact — never the lease record's own checkpoint,\n233|\t// which is null for every epoch-1 owner. Run loads it\n234|\t// through the fold adapter; I/O-free callers supply it by\n235|\t// hand. A successor lease's Checkpoint is the handoff base\n236|\t// and must agree with it.\n237|\tHasNewestCheckpoint bool\n238|\tNewestCheckpointID  string\n239|\n240|\t// Presented is the local fencing token; Observation is the\n241|\t// verified lease view, built by fencing.Observe.\n242|\tPresented   fencing.PresentedToken\n243|\tObservation fencing.Observation\n244|\n245|\t// Backend carries the §4.B identity documents.\n246|\tBackend BackendFacts\n247|\n248|\t// Journal is the loaded materialization journal; JournalOK\n249|\t// reports that the matjournal owner admitted it. When\n250|\t// MaterializationRequired is set (the after-restore step 3),\n251|\t// a local launch additionally requires the committed phase\n252|\t// sourced from the fold's newest published checkpoint. A\n253|\t// fresh launch (§13.1 steps 3-4) runs before the journal\n254|\t// commits and leaves the requirement unset.\n255|\tMaterializationRequired bool\n256|\tJournal                 matjournal.Journal\n257|\tJournalOK               bool\n258|\n259|\t// Checkpoint carries the resume checkpoint: Required when the\n260|\t// path resumes from a checkpoint, Doc with its bytes, ID with\n261|\t// the expected digest. Admission attests through the sessrepo\n262|\t// owner, requires exactly the fold's newest published\n263|\t// checkpoint (with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing\n264|\t// when the winner carries one), and binds the checkpoint's\n265|\t// own session_id to this session.\n266|\tCheckpointRequired bool\n267|\tCheckpointDoc      []byte\n268|\tCheckpointID       string\n269|\n270|\t// ProfileRecord and ProfileEvents are the decoded session\n271|\t// surface the sessprofile reducer derives the effective pair\n272|\t// from. ProfileHeads, when non-empty, is the validated\n273|\t// checkpoint's event-head closure: resume derives from the\n274|\t// closure (DeriveForHeads), never the session head, so a\n275|\t// head-only or losing-lease change cannot become the launch\n276|\t// profile. Run loads the heads from the winner's checkpoint;\n277|\t// I/O-free callers supply them by hand.\n278|\tProfileRecord sessprofile.Record\n279|\tProfileEvents []sessprofile.Event\n280|\tProfileHeads  []string\n281|\n282|\t// Provider carries the probed build, stored identity, and\n283|\t// optional discovery proof.\n284|\tProvider ProviderFacts\n285|\n286|\t// Smoke carries the provider-auth smoke precondition.\n287|\tSmoke SmokeFacts\n288|\n289|\t// Realm carries the caller realm and broker readiness.\n290|\tRealm Realm\n291|\n292|\t// Entrypoint is the wrapper argv, checked against the §4.A\n293|\t// stable entrypoint rule.\n294|\tEntrypoint []string\n295|\n296|\t// Descriptor is the §7.A provider descriptor document the\n297|\t// wrapper supplies; HostBinding is the AX-validated host-local\n298|\t// binding it must match. Admission runs on the launch and\n299|\t// reattach paths only: parked, refused, and remote-offer\n300|\t// outcomes start no local provider.\n301|\tDescriptor  []byte\n302|\tHostBinding terminalbackend.InstanceBinding\n303|\n304|\t// RemoteInteractive reports that the remote owner holds the\n305|\t// session in an interactive terminal (after-restore step 4).\n306|\tRemoteInteractive bool\n307|\n308|\t// Interactive reports that the local pane runs in an\n309|\t// interactive terminal. A non-interactive create must hold the\n310|\t// headless_creation conditional (§4.C create row); the field\n311|\t// selects that arm and shapes the supplied descriptor.\n312|\tInteractive bool\n313|}\n314|\n315|// Decision is the one outcome Decide returns.\n316|type Decision struct {\n317|\t// Action is the outcome.\n318|\tAction Action\n319|\t// ParkReason and WinningLeaseID carry the session.parked\n320|\t// vocabulary when Action is parked. The lease ID is empty when\n321|\t// no winner is established.\n322|\tParkReason     fencing.ParkReason\n323|\tWinningLeaseID string\n324|\t// Class is the Section 15 refusal code when Action is refused.\n325|\tClass string\n326|\t// Detail is the static refusal or park detail. It carries\n327|\t// member names and the landed cause, never credentials,\n328|\t// generations, or native references.\n329|\tDetail string\n330|\t// Cause is the underlying landed error.\n331|\tCause error\n332|\t// Token is the sealed fencing token the passed gate minted,\n333|\t// set on launch and reattach only. The provider receives it\n334|\t// separately from the descriptor (§7.A).\n335|\tToken fencing.LeaseToken\n336|\t// HasToken reports that Token is minted. The zero token never\n337|\t// authorizes: decisions without a passed gate carry none.\n338|\tHasToken bool\n339|\t// Profile is the effective persisted pair the launch carries.\n340|\tProfile sessprofile.Pair\n341|\t// Mapping is the resolved provider adapter flag (empty for\n342|\t// standard).\n343|\tMapping string\n344|\t// Admitted is the reconciled backend capability set.\n345|\tAdmitted terminalbackend.Admitted\n346|\t// Descriptor is the admitted §7.A provider descriptor, set on\n347|\t// launch and reattach only.\n348|\tDescriptor terminalbackend.ProviderDescriptor\n349|\t// RealmFailure is the composed typed Structured Error for the\n350|\t// capability_unavailable and target_auth_missing refusals.\n351|\tRealmFailure *axerror.Error\n352|}\n353|\n354|func refused(class, detail string, cause error) Decision {\n355|\treturn Decision{Action: ActionRefused, Class: class, Detail: detail, Cause: cause}\n356|}\n357|\n358|func parked(reason fencing.ParkReason, winningLeaseID string, cause error) Decision {\n359|\treturn Decision{\n360|\t\tAction:         ActionParked,\n361|\t\tParkReason:     reason,\n362|\t\tWinningLeaseID: winningLeaseID,\n363|\t\tDetail:         \"park (\" + string(reason) + \") without launching the provider\",\n364|\t\tCause:          cause,\n365|\t}\n366|}\n367|\n368|// Decide is the pure wrapper core: configuration, session, bootstrap\n369|// idempotency with the window predicate, backend identity and\n370|// capability admission with the §4.C conditionals, fencing,\n371|// materialization with the fold-newest source binding, checkpoint\n372|// admission bound to the fold newest (with the winning lease's\n373|// handoff base agreeing) and session, provider identity,\n374|// provider-auth smoke with the target binding, realm evidence,\n375|// profile derivation from the checkpoint closure on resume and\n376|// mapping, entrypoint, and provider descriptor, in that\n377|// precedence, then the outcome selection. Fencing precedes\n378|// materialization: a remote owner offers attach/takeover even when\n379|// the local materialization is stale (the after-restore order).\n380|// The tuple gate precedes mapping so a tuple refusal keeps its own\n381|// class instead of wearing profile_mapping_unavailable. Decide\n382|// performs no I/O, reads no clock except the instants the input\n383|// carries, and mints no lease, binding, or event: Run owns the\n384|// durable effects. Every refusal carries the Section 15 code the\n385|// arm names; every park carries the session.parked vocabulary.\n386|func Decide(input Input) Decision {\n387|\tif input.ConfigErr != nil {\n388|\t\treturn refused(ClassInvalidConfig, \"configuration is invalid\", input.ConfigErr)\n389|\t}\n390|\tif input.Mode != ModeLaunch && input.Mode != ModeRestore {\n391|\t\treturn refused(ClassInvalidArguments, \"wrapper mode is not launch or restore\", errWrapperMode(input.Mode))\n392|\t}\n393|\tif !input.SessionKnown {\n394|\t\treturn refused(ClassInvalidArguments, \"logical session is unknown\", errUnknownSession(input.SessionID))\n395|\t}\n396|\tif (input.ExistingBinding == nil || input.ExistingBinding.OperationID != input.BootstrapOperationID) && input.SessionBound && !bootstrapWindowClosed(input) {\n397|\t\treturn refused(terminalbackend.CodeIdempotencyMismatch,\n398|\t\t\t\"bootstrap operation changed inside the bootstrap window\",\n399|\t\t\terrIdempotencyChanged(input.SessionID))\n400|\t}\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
