{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c881","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":667,"recorded_at":1780531400001329,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b197-1751-75d1-8005-04531b754e2a"},"task_id":"01a0b197-1751-75d1-8005-04531b754e2a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b197-1751-75d1-8005-04531b754e2a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/axpane.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through the production entry point), V (verdict from\n11|the Go exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\n12|failure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else —\n13|unapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\n14|infrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file is\n15|restored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\n16|\n17|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n18|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n19|hard-coding kills.\n20|\n21|Usage:\n22|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\n23|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py N-config\n24|\"\"\"\n25|\n26|import os\n27|import shutil\