{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":715,"recorded_at":1780531400001425,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1972847766384c5b1eec4d57764","text":"Read text file `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.5.0, commit\n4|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`, worked against the\n5|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` headings named below (byte-identical\n6|to v0.6.0 in these sections). Primary scope is Sections 4.B-4.D,\n7|4.1-4.2, 5.2 Terminal Events, 5.7 (newest checkpoint), 7.A, and\n8|13.1, plus the 2.4 profile authority the wrapper composes. This\n9|file records implementation evidence; per the Story contract the\n10|`internal/traceability` ownership registry is untouched in this\n11|first leaf — the Story's final leaf carries the registry bindings\n12|and re-pin. This package claims no public CLI delivery: no `ax`\n13|command exists in this tree.\n14|\n15|The wrapper validation core (`internal/axpane`) composes every\n16|check from a landed gate and re-implements none: owner epoch and\n17|fencing from `fencing` (`AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeRestore`,\n18|the sealed `LeaseToken`, the parked vocabulary); the authoritative\n19|newest checkpoint from `sessstate` (`Reduce` over the record with\n20|its authoritative chain: `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`);\n21|materialization validity from `matjournal` (`Store.Get` with its\n22|grammar and cross-reference validation, plus the stated\n23|committed-phase, fold-newest-source, and handoff-agreement rules)\n24|and checkpoint admission from `sessckpt` (`Get`, which re-attests\n25|through `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` on every read) with the\n26|identity, newest, agreement, and session bindings in `Decide`; the\n27|effective persisted profile from `sessprofile` (`DecodeRecord`,\n28|`DecodeEvent`, `Derive`, `DeriveForHeads`) with Section 7.7 mapping\n29|from `provhost` (`ResolveMapping`,\n30|`profile_mapping_unavailable`); provider identity from `provhost`\n31|(`CheckResumeTuple`, `VerifyIdentityBuild`,\n32|`VerifyIdentityDiscovery`, `CreateIdentity` in fixtures) with\n33|`resumesmoke` evidence (`VerifyRecord`) as a precondition input;\n34|backend identity from `terminalbackend` (`ParseManifest`,\n35|`ParseProbe`, `ParseEvidence`, `GenerationDigest`, `Reconcile`,\n36|`CapabilitiesForOperation` via `CheckOperation`, `CheckEntrypoint`,\n37|`AdmitProviderDescriptor`); configuration validity from `config`\n38|(`Load`); session, lease, and event durability from `sessrepo`\n39|(`GetRecord`, `ListEvents`, `ListSessions`, `fencing.Observe` over\n40|`ListLeases`, `AppendEvent`); refusal shapes from `axerror`\n41|(`NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`, `NewTargetAuthMissing`).\n42|\n43|## Acceptance rows\n44|\n45|43 of 43 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below;\n46|the denominator is re-derived by counting this table (43 data\n47|rows), not restated: rev2 claimed \"41 of 41\" while the table has\n48|always held 43 rows, and the independent reviewer measured 39 of\n49|43 faithfully driven. The four unfaithful rev2 rows —\n50|\"Materialization validity gates local resume\", \"Checkpoint\n51|admission gates resume\", \"After-restore sequence 1-5\" (all three\n52|shared the lease-checkpoint keying), and \"Bootstrap idempotency\"\n53|(the superseded receipt) — are re-pinned faithfully in rev3: every\n54|positive carries the chain-published checkpoint the assertions\n55|require, and every negative drives the epoch-1 owner the old\n56|keying admitted. 0 of 43 are delivered as a public CLI surface,\n57|which is an explicit caller-integration bound (no `ax` command\n58|exists in this tree), not a gap in the assigned validation\n59|behavior. Process control, mesh transport, provider supervision,\n60|and backend operations belong to modeled callers and later leaves,\n61|which invoke these entries at every required boundary.\n62|\n63|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n64|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n65|| Lower epoch parks or refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_lower_epoch` | Driven: presented epoch 1 under a winning epoch 2 parks `stale_owner` with the winning lease. |\n66|| Same-epoch loser parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_same_epoch_loser` | Driven: the losing lease at the winning epoch parks `stale_owner`. |\n67|| Future epoch parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_future_epoch` | Driven: an epoch beyond the winner parks `restore_policy`. |\n68|| Foreign session refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_foreign_session` | Driven: a token for another session refuses `lease_conflict`. |\n69|| Expired grant refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_expired_grant` | Driven: a lapsed grant refuses `lease_conflict` on the launch entry. |\n70|| Malformed token refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_malformed_token` | Driven: epoch 0 refuses `invalid_arguments`. |\n71|| Absent winner parks without authority | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Run` skips emission | `TestDecideTable/parked_absent_winner`, `TestRunParkedWithoutWinnerSkipsEmission` | Driven: no winner parks `restore_policy` with an empty lease ID and authors no event, since `session.parked` requires a winning lease. |\n72|| Ambiguous ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_ambiguous` | Driven: conflicting union observations park `restore_policy`. |\n73|| Unverified ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Emit` → `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` refuses | `TestDecideTable/parked_unverified`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_unverified` | Driven: without a proving lease refresh the wrapper parks `restore_policy` with no chain event — the mutation gate refuses unverified emission. |\n74|| Failed handoff parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Emit` → `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` refuses | `TestDecideTable/parked_failed_handoff`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_failed_handoff` | Driven: a losing force lease parks `failed_handoff`, never activates and never emits. |\n75|| Remote interactive owner offers attach | `Decide` → `decideParked` + `terminalbackend.CheckOperation(\"attach\")`; `Run` skips remote emission | `TestDecideTable/attach_remote_interactive` | Driven: a remote winning holder with an interactive terminal and an admitted attach capability offers `attach_remote` with no lease mutation and no chain event under the remote lease. |\n76|| Remote owner otherwise parks or offers takeover | `Decide` → `decideParked`; `Run` skips remote emission | `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_noninteractive`, `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_attach_unproven`, `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission` | Driven: a non-interactive remote owner parks `remote_owner` (§4.2 step 5); an interactive attach-unproven remote owner offers `takeover_offer`. Both start no runtime and author no chain event under the remote lease. |\n77|| Mode selects entry and capability row | `Decide` → `authorize` + `admitBackend` | `TestDecideRestoreRequiresRestoreCapability`, `TestDecideTable/launch_restore_committed_checkpoint` | Driven: restore mode gates through `AuthorizeRestore` and the `restore` row (a restore-admitting, create-denying backend launches); launch mode gates through `AuthorizeActivation` and `create`. |\n78|| Materialization validity gates local resume | `Decide` → `checkMaterialization`; `Run` → `LoadMaterialization` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed`, `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_absent`, `TestDecideMaterializationStaleParks`, `TestDecideJournalNullFoldParks`, `TestDecideJournalLeaseFoldDisagreeParks`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted`, `TestRunRestoreMaterializingParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks` | Driven: a required journal must be admitted by the `matjournal` owner, committed, and sourced from the fold's newest published checkpoint, with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing when the winner carries one; staging, absence, a null fold, a superseded source, or lease/fold disagreement parks `restore_policy`. The epoch-1 owner (null lease checkpoint) parks on an unnamed-digest journal and launches on a newest-sourced one. Fresh launch leaves the requirement unset (§13.1 runs before the journal commits). |\n79|| Checkpoint admission gates resume | `Decide` → `admitCheckpoint` → `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `Run` → `LoadCheckpoint` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_inadmissible`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_wrong_identity`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest`, `TestDecideCheckpointNotLeaseParks`, `TestDecideForeignCheckpointParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointNullFoldParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointUnpublishedParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointLeaseFoldDisagreeParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks` | Driven: a required checkpoint must attest through the `sessrepo` owner, match the required digest, equal the fold's newest published checkpoint with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing when the winner carries one, and name this session; garbage, absence, identity drift, a null fold, an unpublished checkpoint, a non-newest checkpoint, lease/fold disagreement, or a foreign session parks `restore_policy`. |\n80|| Effective profile derived with source | `Decide` → `deriveProfile` → `sessprofile.Derive`/`DeriveForHeads`; `Run` → `LoadProfile` + winner closure | `TestDecideProfileSourcePinsEvent`, `TestDecideYoloMapping`, `TestDecideResumeProfileUsesClosure`, `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored`, `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails` | Driven: launch carries the session head (newest authoritative `profile.changed` with that event's digest, or the record value with null source); resume carries the validated checkpoint's event-head closure (`DeriveForHeads`), so a head-only or losing-lease change never becomes the launch profile (PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME direction). A winner that carries a checkpoint with no checkpoint store bound fails the run — an absent store is unknown, never \"no closure\". Corrupt derivation refuses `integrity_failure` (`TestDecideTable/refused_profile_derivation_corrupt`). |\n81|| Profile mapping resolved or refused | `Decide` → `provhost.ResolveMapping` | `TestDecideYoloMapping`, `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_mapping_unavailable` | Driven: the yolo launch carries the exact codex adapter flag; a Pi build off the pinned version refuses `profile_mapping_unavailable` per §2.4. The tuple gate precedes mapping so a tuple refusal keeps its own class. |\n82|| Resume tuple gate | `Decide` → `checkProviderIdentity` → `provhost.CheckResumeTuple` | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_tuple_qwen` | Driven: a tuple outside the §8.4 direction refuses `invalid_config` with the landed detail. |\n83|| Identity bind to exact build | `Decide` → `provhost.VerifyIdentityBuild` | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_identity_other_provider` | Driven: an identity minted for another provider (`CreateIdentity` fixture) refuses `invalid_config`; the probed version must equal the record version exactly. |\n84|| Discovery bind | `Decide` → `provhost.VerifyIdentityDiscovery` | `TestDecideTable/launch_discovery_bound`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_native_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_root_outside`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_empty_home` | Driven: a proof binding the identity's native ID under the §8.2 store root launches; native drift, an outside root, or an empty home refuse `invalid_config`. |\n85|| Provider-auth smoke precondition | `Decide` → `checkSmoke` → `resumesmoke.VerifyRecord` + `axerror.NewTargetAuthMissing` | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_failing_verdict`, `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_absent`, `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_wrong_build`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/target_auth_missing_details`, `TestRunSmokeRequiredPasses`, `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence/stale_generation_with_realm_refuses` | Driven: a required smoke must verify, pass, bind the exact probed build, and bind the current generation with the probed OS version in the typed target; failure, absence, build drift, or a stale generation/version refuses `target_auth_missing` with the typed §15.3 details. |\n86|| Backend identity admission | `Decide` → `admitBackend` → `terminalbackend.ParseManifest/ParseProbe/ParseEvidence/Reconcile` | `TestDecideLaunchPositive` | Driven: a real manifest/probe/RSA-signed-evidence universe reconciles and admits `headless_creation` for `create` (and `reboot_restoration` for `restore`, `local_attach` for `attach`). |\n87|| Mismatch fails before activation | `Decide` → `admitBackend` | `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_protocol_membership`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_generation_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_evidence_expired`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_signature_untrusted` | Driven: protocol drift refuses `terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch`; generation drift refuses the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation`; expired evidence refuses; an untrusted signature refuses `terminal_backend_integrity_failure`. |\n88|| Only admitted rows authorize | `Decide` → `terminalbackend.CheckOperation` + headless conditional | `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_capability_unproven`, `TestDecideNonInteractiveRequiresHeadless` | Driven: with no admitted capability conferring `create`, the wrapper refuses `terminal_backend_capability_unproven`; a non-interactive create without `headless_creation` refuses even when another row confers `create`. No capability map is invented: the `Reconcile` set is the only authority. |\n89|| Background caller without attested server | `Decide` → `checkRealm` → `terminalbackend.Reconcile` + `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/capability_unavailable_details`, `TestDecideTable/launch_background_attested_server`, `TestDecideRealmBindingMismatchRefuses`, `TestDecideForegroundCredentialRequiresRealm`, `TestDecideRealmEvidenceOrderIndependent`, `TestDecideExpiredRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecidePreRebootRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecideLiveRealmRowBackendFaultStands` | Driven: a background caller, and any caller on a credential-requiring path (§4.C conditional rows), authorizes only through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to the host binding, probed build, and current generation; without it (or with a mismatched binding/build or stale generation) it refuses `capability_unavailable` with typed details and never creates a server. An expired or pre-reboot realm row refuses the same typed refusal (the reconcile failure is the cause); an unrelated backend fault with a usable realm row keeps its own class; the cross-bind accepts when any realm object binds, in either evidence order. Incomplete typed details refuse `invalid_arguments` (`TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_incomplete_details`). |\n90|| Cached evidence never authorizes | `Decide` → `checkRealm` + `checkSmoke` (behavioral) | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence`, `TestDecideForegroundCredentialRequiresRealm` | Driven: a background caller with a passing (cached) smoke record but no admitted realm row refuses, as does a foreground caller on a credential-requiring path; with a stale generation refuses; only the admitted row bound to the current generation, host binding, and probed build launches — no cached sentinel, `managername`, or boolean authorizes. |\n91|| Bootstrap idempotency | `Store.Bind`/`Supersede`/`Lookup`/`SessionBound`, `Decide` (windowed idempotency arm), `Run` | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestDecidePostWindowNewOperationLaunches`, `TestDecideWindowEpochOneOwnerCloses`, `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair`, `TestBindIdenticalRetryReattaches`, `TestBindChangedOperationRefusesMismatch`, `TestBindSweepsStaleStaging`, `TestBindConcurrentSameOperationReattaches`, `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestSupersedeKeepsReceipts`, `TestSupersedeConcurrentDifferentOps`, `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays`, `TestLookupSessionMismatchRefuses`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunConcurrentLaunchReattaches`, `TestRunIdempotencyMismatch`, `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`, `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`, `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` | Driven: a changed operation inside the bootstrap window (the fold names no newest checkpoint) refuses `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes; an identical retry of any recorded pair replays its own receipt (the stored receipt is authoritative, superseded pairs keep theirs); a concurrent same-operation commit reattaches while a changed-operation commit refuses; after the window closes a new operation records its own pair receipt no-replace and launches, in both modes. Stale pre-commit staging is swept. |\n92|| Status proves absence or the one child | `Store.Status` + `Store.Lookup` | `TestBindInstallsAndStatusProves`, `TestStatusSessionMismatchRefuses`, `TestLookupSessionMismatchRefuses`, `TestSupersedeKeepsReceipts` | Driven: absence proves only when no binding exists; `Status` identifies the first-binding anchor while `Lookup` replays each pair's own receipt; a receipt read under another session or operation refuses even with a shared prefix. |\n93|| Unknown is not absent | `Store.Status`/`Lookup`/`SessionBound`, `Run` → `ObserveOwnership` | `TestStatusUnknownIsNotAbsent`, `TestRunTornBindingPropagates`, `TestRunTornLeasePropagates` | Driven: a torn anchor fails `Status` and `SessionBound`, a torn pair receipt fails `Lookup` and the identical retry, and a torn lease fails `ObserveOwnership`, each propagating through `Run` with no decision — never absence, never a parked cover, never a launch. |\n94|| Crash at the binding seam | `Store.Bind`/`Supersede` + `Hooks` | `TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`, `TestBindHookAfterStageAbortsWithoutInstall`, `TestBindHookAfterInstallKeepsTheCommit`, `TestSupersedeCrashSeams` | Driven: a real SIGKILL after the no-replace commit leaves the complete binding and the identical retry reattaches; an aborted stage leaves absence the retry converges from; a post-commit hook error keeps the commit, on both the anchor and the pair-receipt paths. |\n95|| No PID persisted | `Store.Bind` (closed receipt) | `TestBindingPersistsNoPID` | Driven: the stored bytes carry exactly the seven closed members — UUIDv7 instance plus opaque digest — and no PID/handle/socket/endpoint/token member. |\n96|| Stable entrypoint | `Decide` → `terminalbackend.CheckEntrypoint` | `TestDecideTable/refused_entrypoint_raw_provider` | Driven: a raw provider argv refuses `local_precondition_failed`; only `ax pane SESSION_ID` passes. |\n97|| §7.A descriptor supplied and admitted | `BuildDescriptor`, `Decide` → `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` | `TestDescriptorBuildAdmitRoundTrip`, `TestDescriptorMismatchRefuses`, `TestDescriptorGenerationBounds`, `TestDecideTable/refused_descriptor_generation_drift` | Driven: the wrapper supplies the closed descriptor (fresh UUIDv7 instance, never a PID) and admits it against the validated host-local binding before any launch effect — parse, match, then launch, with no caching across the check. Binding, version, and generation drift refuse; generation lengths 0 and 257 refuse while 256 admits. |\n98|| Fencing token passed separately | `Decide` (token projection) → `fencing.LeaseToken.Bind` | `TestDecideLaunchPositive`, `TestDecideForgedTokensRefuse`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` | Driven: launch and reattach carry the sealed token minted by the passed gate, binding `quiesce`/`capture`/`materialize` to the winning triple; parked, refused, and offer decisions carry the zero token, which refuses every provider operation. |\n99|| `session.parked` authored under lease | `EmitParked` → `Emit` → `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` + `sessstate.Reduce` + `sessrepo.AppendEvent`; `Run` pre-checks | `TestEmitParkedRoundTrip`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop`, `TestEmitParkedUnfoldableRefuses`, `TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses`, `TestRunParkedEmits`, `TestRunParkedUnfoldableSkipsEmission`, `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission`, `TestEmitParkedRefusesNonParked` | Driven: verified, locally held, foldable parks author the exact closed payload under the winning lease with current chain linkage (every `Emit` gates through `AuthorizeMutation`; `session.parked` folds only from materializing/stopped/failed/parked); a losing presented tuple refuses at the mutation gate itself (`not_owner` under a remote winner, `stale_owner` under a local successor) on a foldable chain; remote, unverified, and unfolderable parks author nothing rather than manufacturing a collision; launch and refused decisions emit nothing, and emission for a non-parked decision refuses. |\n100|| v4 terminal payloads | `TerminalCreatedPayload`, `ResumedPayload`, `Emit` | `TestTerminalCreatedPayload`, `TestResumedPayload`, `TestEmitTerminalV4RoundTrip` | Driven: both v4 payloads carry exactly the §5.2 members (opaque binding digest, backend identity, evidence IDs; checkpoint plus effective profile pair for resumed), append under schema 4.0.0, and read back; malformed members refuse. |\n101|| §13.1 step 3 durable entry before launch | `Run` → `Store.Bind` | `TestRunLaunchBinds`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted` | Driven: the bootstrap pair binds durably before the launch outcome returns; the binding names the launched instance. Provider launch itself is a later leaf (stated bound). |\n102|| §13.1 step 4 validated plan | `Decide` (mapping + descriptor + token) | `TestLaunchCarriesValidatedPlan` | Driven: every launch carries the resolved adapter mapping, the admitted descriptor, and the sealed token together — no partial plan. Provider argv/env supervision is a later leaf (stated bound). |\n103|| Configuration validated | `Run` → `ValidateConfig` → `config.Load`; `Decide` (config arm) | `TestDecideTable/refused_config_invalid`, `TestRunInvalidConfig` | Driven: a failing configuration load refuses `invalid_config` through the real loader. |\n104|| Session loaded | `Run` → `LoadSession`; `Decide` (session arm) | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_session`, `TestRunUnknownSession` | Driven: an unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`; observation is skipped without a session. |\n105|| After-restore sequence 1-5 | `Decide` in restore mode; `Run` → `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideAfterRestoreSequence`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideWindowEpochOneOwnerCloses`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint` | Driven: winning lease plus valid required materialization resumes, with the window, admission, and journal all keyed on the fold's newest published checkpoint; materializing, unverified, and lease-absent inputs park per steps 3 and 5; interactive remote owners offer per step 4 and non-interactive remote owners park per step 5; authorize precedes materialization. The bounded mesh refresh of step 2 is the caller-reported `Verified` fact (stated bound: no network here). |\n106|| Arm precedence | `Decide` | `TestDecideArmPrecedence` | Driven: an all-faulted input refuses at the configuration arm first; peeling faults walks the documented order. |\n107|| Orchestrated effects | `Run` | `TestRunLaunchBinds`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunParkedEmits`, `TestRunParkedUnfoldableSkipsEmission`, `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission`, `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`, `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`, `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks`, `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails`, `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestRunRefusedWritesNothing`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` | Driven: exactly one effect per outcome — launch binds (recording its own pair receipt post-window), reattach returns the pair receipt, locally held foldable parks emit while remote/unfolderable parks emit nothing, refused writes nothing; ownership observes the real winning lease, the fold supplies the newest checkpoint, and the run fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store; torn leases propagate with no decision. |\n108|\n109|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n110|\n111|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays\n112|present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it\n113|must reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the\n114|delivered harness (`internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, run as\n115|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3\n116|internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`). Whole-arm deletes are not\n117|accepted as narrowing. The `C-` row is the applied harmless\n118|SURVIVED control. Verdicts below are from the evidence run\n119|(`mutants.log` in the producer evidence archive): 48 of 48 rows\n120|match, 47 KILLED plus the SURVIVED control.\n121|\n122|| Mutant | Weakening (one member admitted) | Killer test | Verdict |\n123|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n124|| N-config | Invalid config admitted on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/refused_config_invalid` | KILLED |\n125|| N-mode | Empty mode admitted; other non-modes refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_empty_mode` | KILLED |\n126|| N-session | Unknown session admitted on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_session` | KILLED |\n127|| N-idempotency | Changed operation admitted on launch mode only (in-window) | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch` | KILLED |\n128|| N-idempotency-restore | Changed operation admitted on restore mode only (in-window) | `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses` | KILLED |\n129|| N-idempotency-bound | Unrecorded pairs on bound sessions admitted, requiring a mismatched receipt | `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses` | KILLED |\n130|| N-window-fold | Window closed on launch mode without a published checkpoint | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch` | KILLED |\n131|| N-caller | `batch` caller admitted; other non-callers refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_caller` | KILLED |\n132|| N-backend-op | Restore-mode callers admitted to the create row | `TestDecideRestoreRequiresRestoreCapability` | KILLED |\n133|| N-materialization | Staging journals admitted; absent and other phases park | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed` | KILLED |\n134|| N-materialization-source | Stale source generation admitted; other stale sources park | `TestDecideMaterializationStaleParks` | KILLED |\n135|| N-materialization-nullfold | Restore-mode journals past the null-fold arm (wrong cause surfaces) | `TestDecideJournalNullFoldParks` | KILLED |\n136|| N-materialization-agreement | Restore-mode journals under a disagreeing lease admitted | `TestDecideJournalLeaseFoldDisagreeParks` | KILLED |\n137|| N-checkpoint-nullfold | Restore-mode checkpoints past the null-fold arm (wrong cause surfaces) | `TestDecideCheckpointNullFoldParks` | KILLED |\n138|| N-checkpoint-agreement | Restore-mode checkpoints under a disagreeing lease admitted | `TestDecideCheckpointLeaseFoldDisagreeParks` | KILLED |\n139|| N-checkpoint-absent | Absent checkpoints admitted; bad bytes still park | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent` | KILLED |\n140|| N-checkpoint-prefix | Same-prefix digests admitted; full compare otherwise | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest` | KILLED |\n141|| N-checkpoint-newest | Restore-mode non-newest checkpoints admitted; launch still parks | `TestDecideCheckpointNotLeaseParks` | KILLED |\n142|| N-checkpoint-session | Foreign fixture session admitted; other foreign still park | `TestDecideForeignCheckpointParks` | KILLED |\n143|| N-identity-version | 0.147.0 identity mismatches admitted; other versions refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_identity_other_provider` | KILLED |\n144|| N-discovery | Empty-home discovery admitted; other proofs still verify | `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_empty_home` | KILLED |\n145|| N-smoke-verdict | Failing verdicts admitted; gated/unsupported/unknown refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_failing_verdict` | KILLED |\n146|| N-smoke-version | Version drift admitted; provider/platform/arch still bind | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_wrong_build` | KILLED |\n147|| N-smoke-mode | Required smoke skipped on launch only | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_absent` | KILLED |\n148|| N-profile-derive | Corrupt derivation admitted for codex (wrong class surfaces) | `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_derivation_corrupt` | KILLED |\n149|| N-profile-closure | Session head derived instead of closure on restore only | `TestDecideResumeProfileUsesClosure` | KILLED |\n150|| N-mapping | Standard mapping gaps admitted; yolo gaps refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_mapping_unavailable` | KILLED |\n151|| N-realm | Broker-running background callers admitted; other states refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server` | KILLED |\n152|| N-realm-foreground | Foreground credential-requiring callers admitted without the realm row | `TestDecideForegroundCredentialRequiresRealm` | KILLED |\n153|| N-realm-deadmap | Launch-mode dead-realm evidence admitted to the backend class | `TestDecideExpiredRealmRowRefusesUnavailable` | KILLED |\n154|| N-realm-binding | Mismatched test binding admitted; other mismatches refuse | `TestDecideRealmBindingMismatchRefuses/binding` | KILLED |\n155|| N-realm-generation | Stale test generation admitted; other stale refuse | `TestDecideRealmBindingMismatchRefuses/generation` | KILLED |\n156|| N-headless | Durable-holding non-interactive without headless admitted | `TestDecideNonInteractiveRequiresHeadless` | KILLED |\n157|| N-entrypoint | Two-element argv admitted; other arities refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_entrypoint_raw_provider` | KILLED |\n158|| N-descriptor | Launch-mode descriptor mismatch admitted; restore refuses | `TestDecideTable/refused_descriptor_generation_drift` | KILLED |\n159|| N-attach | Remote attach without the capability admitted | `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_attach_unproven` | KILLED |\n160|| N-reattach | Launch selected over reattach on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair` | KILLED |\n161|| N-binding-prefix | Same-prefix changed operations admitted at the race | `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses` | KILLED |\n162|| N-binding-session | Same-prefix foreign sessions admitted at status | `TestStatusSessionMismatchRefuses` | KILLED |\n163|| N-bind-first | Changed test operation admitted past the anchor pre-check (wrong error surfaces) | `TestBindChangedOperationRefusesMismatch` | KILLED |\n164|| N-supersede-no-replace | Test pair receipt replaced on the commit race | `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays` | KILLED |\n165|| N-parked-reason | Five-letter reasons admitted; vocabulary otherwise closed | `TestParkedPayloadVocabulary` | KILLED |\n166|| N-emit-mutation | Unverified emissions admitted; verified refusals refuse | `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_unverified` | KILLED |\n167|| N-emit-losing-epoch | Losing-epoch emissions admitted; same-or-winning-epoch refusals refuse | `TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses` | KILLED |\n168|| N-parked-fold | Unfolderable restore_policy admitted; other unfolderable refuse | `TestEmitParkedUnfoldableRefuses` | KILLED |\n169|| N-run-fold | Run admits unfolderable restore_policy; other still skip | `TestRunParkedUnfoldableSkipsEmission` | KILLED |\n170|| N-run-ckpt-store | Launch-mode runs with a checkpoint-carrying winner and no store admitted | `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails` | KILLED |\n171|| C-doc-comment | Comment-only control edit | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | SURVIVED |\n172|\n173|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: this package\n174|contains no gate that inspects source text, so the additional\n175|behavioral-suite mutant the evidence contract names for such gates\n176|has no target here. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call in\n177|`checkProviderIdentity` is fail-fast ordering over the same gate\n178|`VerifyIdentityBuild` enforces internally, so weakening it alone is\n179|unobservable by construction; likewise the `admitted.Has` realm\n180|pre-check is fail-fast before the evidence cross-bind, so weakening\n181|it alone is unobservable and the binding mutants cover the gate;\n182|the N-identity-version mutant covers the provider-identity gate as\n183|a whole. The fencing entry selection (`AuthorizeRestore` vs\n184|`AuthorizeActivation`) shares one launch-class core in the\n185|`fencing` owner, so no behavioral delta exists to mutate; the\n186|mode-selected backend capability row carries the mode mutant\n187|(N-backend-op).\n188|\n189|## Crash and idempotency evidence\n190|\n191|The bootstrap binding is the only durable write. Every receipt\n192|installs under the landed discipline: same-directory staging,\n193|0600, fsync, atomic link as the no-replace commit, staging\n194|cleanup, directory fsync (skipped, never faked, on Windows).\n195|Readers see absence or the complete receipt, never a torn prefix.\n196|The session's first binding anchors the in-window contention and\n197|every recorded pair keeps its own receipt, so post-window pairs\n198|record alongside — never over — their superseded receipts; a crash\n199|between the anchor and pair installs converges the pair from the\n200|anchor bytes on retry. Crash hooks arm both boundaries\n201|(`AfterStage` before the commit, `AfterInstall` after it) on both\n202|install paths; the real-kill test\n203|(`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`) SIGKILLs the child between\n204|commit and directory sync and proves the complete binding plus a\n205|converging identical retry. Parked events append through the\n206|`sessrepo` owner, whose own crash evidence stays with that\n207|package; this leaf proves linkage and round-trip only.\n208|\n209|## Stated bounds\n210|\n211|- No `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n212|  process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n213|  broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive\n214|  as `Decide` inputs) and later leaves.\n215|- The bounded mesh lease refresh (after-restore step 2) is the\n216|  caller-reported `Verified` fact, not a network call.\n217|- Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n218|  `terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier`; tests authenticate through\n219|  a generated RSA key.\n220|- Backend liveness (`terminal_backend_unavailable` at the\n221|  operation call site) belongs to the later backend-operation\n222|  leaf: no backend operation exists here, so no availability rule\n223|  is invented.\n224|- The host-local `InstanceBinding` the descriptor must match\n225|  arrives from the modeled backend caller; the wrapper proves\n226|  document-to-binding consistency and never mints backend\n227|  bindings.\n228|- The committed-phase rule for a required materialization is the\n229|  wrapper's stated reading of after-restore step 3 (\"the required\n230|  materialization is valid\").\n231|- Invalid materialization or checkpoint on an otherwise winning\n232|  local owner parks `restore_policy` per the literal step-5\n233|  reading (\"enter parked without launching the provider in all\n234|  other cases\"), with the blocking cause in the decision detail.\n235|- Unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`: the call names\n236|  no logical session. No `unknown_session` wire code is minted.\n237|- The dead-realm refusal mapping applies only when the caller\n238|  needs the realm row and submitted at least one realm evidence\n239|  object that is unusable (expired or bound to a superseded\n240|  generation). With no submitted realm row, or any usable one, a\n241|  reconcile failure keeps its backend class.\n242|- The realm cross-bind accepts when any submitted realm object\n243|  binds this host and build: order-independent by scan, pinned in\n244|  both evidence orders plus the all-foreign refusal.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
