{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cabf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":954,"recorded_at":1780531400001903,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b197bf4f700e97cdd54eaf5c54ec","text":"Read text file `/tmp/results-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj rev3 — producer results\n2|\n3|Task: implement `ax pane` SESSION_ID enforcement wrapper\n4|(rev3 rework of review-verdict-rev2: 1 P1 class, 2 P2, 8 P3).\n5|Trunk: `2fc6d50` (`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, headings\n6|byte-identical to v0.6.0 in scope). Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in\n7|the Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n8|\n9|## Pre-existing worktree state (partial-attempt recovery)\n10|\n11|On entry the worktree already held the rev2 candidate UNCOMMITTED:\n12|untracked `internal/axpane/` plus additive hunks in `LOGBOOK.md`\n13|(+17) and `README.md` (+56). No commit existed past the\n14|checkpoint. I read `TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev2.md`\n15|(CHANGES REQUESTED) and the review-evidence archive before\n16|touching code, then ran\n17|`task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-1geqhj` →\n18|`refresh_advanced`, trunk `2fc6d50`. The refresh left old-base\n19|content in trunk-moved paths, so I restored `HEAD` content for\n20|every trunk-moved path and re-applied only my additive hunks\n21|(verified: `git diff` shows 0 deletions across `LOGBOOK.md` /\n22|`README.md`, `task-board.config.json` == `HEAD`). Final\n23|`git status`: `M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n24|`?? internal/axpane/` — candidate paths only.\n25|\n26|## Root-cause fixes (production call sites)\n27|\n28|- P1-1 (window/admission/journal keying): the window predicate,\n29|  checkpoint admission, and journal source binding read the chain\n30|  fold's newest checkpoint (`Input.HasNewestCheckpoint` /\n31|  `NewestCheckpointID`, loaded by `Run` via\n32|  `LoadNewestCheckpoint` → `loadFoldInput` + `sessstate.Reduce`),\n33|  never `Winner.HasCheckpoint`/`Winner.Checkpoint`. A successor\n34|  lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\n35|  (`leaseCheckpointAgrees`, `decide.go`); disagreement or a null\n36|  fold with a requirement parks `restore_policy`. A null fold\n37|  parks; the only launch-class path left in that state is the\n38|  bootstrap retry without a checkpoint.\n39|- P2-1 (receipt retention): the store keeps one receipt per pair\n40|  (`Store.Lookup`, `receipts/<op>.json`, no-replace link commit)\n41|  with `binding.json` as the first-binding anchor;\n42|  `Store.Supersede` is no-replace per pair plus anchor claim, and\n43|  `Store.SessionBound` (anchor-or-receipts) drives the\n44|  changed-operation arm with the fold window. All four §4.1\n45|  vectors hold: any recorded pair replays, concurrent\n46|  different-op supersedes each record, identical retry replays.\n47|- P2-2 (unknown checkpoint store): `Run` fails when the winner\n48|  carries a checkpoint and `stores.Ckpt == nil` (`run.go`,\n49|  mirroring the `CheckpointRequired` guard) — an absent store is\n50|  unknown, never \"no closure\".\n51|- P3-1: losing-lease emission test uses a foldable (failed) chain\n52|  and asserts the `AuthorizeMutation` refusal itself (`not_owner`\n53|  remote, `stale_owner` local successor), plus the `N-emit-losing-epoch`\n54|  (RV7) narrowing row.\n55|- P3-2: launch-mode create-from-stopped post-window restore\n56|  through `Run` (`TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow`).\n57|- P3-3: ratio re-derived by counting: 43/43 (see below).\n58|- P3-4: the §4.C credential conditional applies to every caller\n59|  with `Smoke.Required`, not only background (`checkRealm`).\n60|- P3-5: the realm cross-bind accepts when ANY realm object binds\n61|  (`checkRealmBinding` scans; pinned in both evidence orders).\n62|- P3-6: dead (expired/pre-reboot) realm evidence refuses the\n63|  typed `capability_unavailable` with the reconcile failure as\n64|  cause (`deadRealmRefusal`); a usable row plus an unrelated\n65|  backend fault keeps the backend class (pinned).\n66|- P3-7: misleading test renamed to\n67|  `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission`;\n68|  `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes` rewritten (sourced journal,\n69|  chain-published checkpoint, `Lookup` assertions).\n70|- P3-8: the rev2 LOGBOOK entry explicitly reverses rev1 F1\n71|  (remote offers author nothing).\n72|\n73|## AC coverage: 43 of 43 rows driven\n74|\n75|Every row of the acceptance table in\n76|`internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md` (43 data rows, counted) is\n77|driven through the production entry named in its call-site\n78|column: `Decide` (pure core), `Run` (orchestration), `EmitParked`\n79|/ `Emit`, `Store.Bind` / `Supersede` / `Lookup` / `SessionBound` /\n80|`Status`, `LoadNewestCheckpoint`, `LoadCheckpoint`,\n81|`LoadMaterialization`, `LoadProfile`, `ObserveOwnership`,\n82|`AdmitProviderDescriptor`, `BuildDescriptor`. The four rows the\n83|reviewer measured unfaithful in rev2 (materialization validity,\n84|checkpoint admission, after-restore sequence, bootstrap\n85|idempotency) are re-pinned: positives carry the chain-published\n86|checkpoint; negatives drive the epoch-1 owner.\n87|`TestConformanceMatrixCompleteness` pins the clause→test map\n88|(extended with 5.7 newest, per-pair retention, credential\n89|conditional, dead-realm, order-independence, unknown-store rows).\n90|\n91|## Negative and mutant evidence\n92|\n93|- 21 new committed tests in `internal/axpane/rev3_test.go` plus\n94|  re-pinned positives; every gate ships narrowing mutants.\n95|- `mutant_harness.py`: 48/48 rows match — 47 KILLED + the\n96|  SURVIVED control, with raw per-plant logs and subprocess exits\n97|  in `mutants.log` (evidence tar). New rows: `N-window-fold`,\n98|  `N-checkpoint-nullfold`, `N-materialization-nullfold`,\n99|  `N-checkpoint-newest`, `N-checkpoint-agreement`,\n100|  `N-materialization-agreement`, `N-idempotency-bound`,\n101|  `N-realm-foreground`, `N-realm-deadmap`,\n102|  `N-supersede-no-replace`, `N-run-ckpt-store`,\n103|  `N-emit-losing-epoch`, `N-bind-first`.\n104|- Crash/idempotency: no-replace link commits on both install\n105|  paths, hook-armed seams, real-SIGKILL test, anchor→pair crash\n106|  convergence; parked events append through the `sessrepo`\n107|  owner (linkage/round-trip proven here).\n108|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate\n109|  inspects source text.\n110|\n111|## Validation suite (task-board.config.json, in order)\n112|\n113|| # | Command | Exit |\n114|| --- | --- | --- |\n115|| 1 | `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 |\n116|| 2 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (axpane 80.6%) |\n117|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n118|| 4 | `gofmt -l $(git ls-files '*.go')` | 0 (empty; plus `gofmt -l internal/axpane` clean for untracked) |\n119|| 5 | `go test -race ./... -count=1` | 0 |\n120|| 6–8 | catalog consistency/docs/capability-docs | 0/0/0 |\n121|| 9 | doctor bundle | 1 — PRE-EXISTING: `internal/doctor` absent at HEAD `2fc6d50` (setup failure, no package to load); unrelated to this candidate, which adds no doctor surface |\n122|| 10–15 | traceability projection/docs/ownership, specdoc, v06, v07 | 0 ×6 |\n123|| 16–18 | bundle install scripts | skipped-dirty, exit 0 (cmd16 additionally never arms: `DIRTY` unset in the suite) |\n124|| 19–27 | catalog locking/concurrency/tx, provhost ×3, terminalbackend ×3 | 0 ×9 |\n125|\n126|Full logs in\n127|`.temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/rev3-evidence.tar.gz` (`cmd01`–`cmd27`,\n128|`mutants.log`, manifest with SHAs, candidate diff).\n129|\n130|## Files changed\n131|\n132|- `internal/axpane/` (new package): `decide.go`, `run.go`,\n133|  `binding.go`, `events.go`, `gates.go`, `errors.go`, `doc.go`,\n134|  `descriptor.go`, `sync.go`, `*_test.go` (incl. new\n135|  `rev3_test.go`), `TRACEABILITY.md`, `mutant_harness.py`.\n136|- `README.md`: package section (additive, updated to rev3).\n137|- `LOGBOOK.md`: rev3 entry + explicit rev1-F1 reversal (additive).\n138|\n139|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n140|\n141|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added;\n142|mesh refresh is the caller-reported `Verified` fact; the\n143|dead-realm mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm\n144|row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable; tuple-gate\n145|defense-in-depth is stated in TRACEABILITY.md. `internal/traceability`\n146|untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n147|\n148|## Handoff\n149|\n150|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n151|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n152|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_results-rev3.md`,\n153|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix-rev3.md`,\n154|`rev3-evidence.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
