\\\\n\\\\t\\\\treturn nil, errCheckpointLeaseDisagree()\\\\n\\\\t}\\\\n\\\",\\ninternal/axpane/mutant_harness.py:197:        run=\\\"TestDecideCheckpointLeaseFoldDisagreeParks\\\",\\ninternal/axpane/mutant_harness.py:572:        run=\\\"TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails\\\",\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:23:committed-phase, fold-newest-source, and handoff-agreement rules)\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:78:| Materialization validity gates local resume | `Decide` → `checkMaterialization`; `Run` → `LoadMaterialization` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed`, `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_absent`, `TestDecideMaterializationStaleParks`, `TestDecideJournalNullFoldParks`, `TestDecideJournalLeaseFoldDisagreeParks`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted`, `TestRunRestoreMaterializingParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks` | Driven: a required journal must be admitted by the `matjournal` owner, committed, and sourced from the fold's newest published checkpoint, with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing when the winner carries one; staging, absence, a null fold, a superseded source, or lease/fold disagreement parks `restore_policy`. The epoch-1 owner (null lease checkpoint) parks on an unnamed-digest journal and launches on a newest-sourced one. Fresh launch leaves the requirement unset (§13.1 runs before the journal commits). |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:79:| Checkpoint admission gates resume | `Decide` → `admitCheckpoint` → `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `Run` → `LoadCheckpoint` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_inadmissible`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_wrong_identity`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest`, `TestDecideCheckpointNotLeaseParks`, `TestDecideForeignCheckpointParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointNullFoldParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointUnpublishedParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointLeaseFoldDisagreeParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks` | Driven: a required checkpoint must attest through the `sessrepo` owner, match the required digest, equal the fold's newest published checkpoint with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing when the winner carries one, and name this session; garbage, absence, identity drift, a null fold, an unpublished checkpoint, a non-newest checkpoint, lease/fold disagreement, or a foreign session parks `restore_policy`. |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:80:| Effective profile derived with source | `Decide` → `deriveProfile` → `sessprofile.Derive`/`DeriveForHeads`; `Run` → `LoadProfile` + winner closure | `TestDecideProfileSourcePinsEvent`, `TestDecideYoloMapping`, `TestDecideResumeProfileUsesClosure`, `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored`, `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails` | Driven: launch carries the session head (newest authoritative `profile.changed` with that event's digest, or the record value with null source); resume carries the validated checkpoint's event-head closure (`DeriveForHeads`), so a head-only or losing-lease change never becomes the launch profile (PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME direction). A winner that carries a checkpoint with no checkpoint store bound fails the run — an absent store is unknown, never \\\"no closure\\\". Corrupt derivation refuses `integrity_failure` (`TestDecideTable/refused_profile_derivation_corrupt`). |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:107:| Orchestrated effects | `Run` | `TestRunLaunchBinds`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunParkedEmits`, `TestRunParkedUnfoldableSkipsEmission`, `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission`, `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`, `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`, `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks`, `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails`, `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestRunRefusedWritesNothing`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` | Driven: exactly one effect per outcome — launch binds (recording its own pair receipt post-window), reattach returns the pair receipt, locally held foldable parks emit while remote/unfolderable parks emit nothing, refused writes nothing; ownership observes the real winning lease, the fold supplies the newest checkpoint, and the run fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store; torn leases propagate with no decision. |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:136:| N-materialization-agreement | Restore-mode journals under a disagreeing lease admitted | `TestDecideJournalLeaseFoldDisagreeParks` | KILLED |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:138:| N-checkpoint-agreement | Restore-mode checkpoints under a disagreeing lease admitted | `TestDecideCheckpointLeaseFoldDisagreeParks` | KILLED |\\ninternal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md:170:| N-run-ckpt-store | Launch-mode runs with a checkpoint-carrying winner and no store admitted | `TestRunNoCkptStoreWinnerCheckpointFails` | KILLED |\\nREADME.md:2164:`sessckpt`/`sessrepo` with the winning lease's handoff base agreeing, the\\nLOGBOOK.md:9:- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev2 (1 P1 class, 2 P2, 8 P3): the bootstrap window, checkpoint admission, and journal source binding now read the chain fold's newest checkpoint (`sessstate.Reduce` → `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`) instead of the lease record's checkpoint, which is null for every epoch-1 owner; a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold; superseded pairs keep per-operation receipts (`receipts/<op>.json`, no-replace per pair) with the first binding as the in-window anchor; `Run` fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store bound; the §4.C credential conditional applies to every caller with `Smoke.Required`, the realm cross-bind accepts any binding object, and dead (expired/pre-reboot) realm evidence refuses the typed `capability_unavailable`.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6579,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1645,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
