: N-window-lease-checkpoint: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Closes the window on the lease record's checkpoint while the fold names none; the null-fold changed op launches instead of refusing. [exit 1]\\nok: N-run-fold-error: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Launders an unfoldable chain as a null fold; Run parks instead of failing with the fold error. [exit 1]\\nok: N-supersede-replay: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Keeps launch on the post-window replay exactly in restore mode; launch-mode replays still reattach. [exit 1]\\nok: N-identity-session: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the foreign fixture session's identity record; other foreign sessions still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-run-newest-absent: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly restore-mode runs with the newest absent from the store (the head pair launches); launch-mode still fails. [exit 1]\\nok: N-emit-losing-epoch: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly losing-epoch emissions; same-or-winning-epoch refusals still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: C-doc-comment: SURVIVED (want SURVIVED) :: Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive. [exit 0]\\nMISMATCHES: 0\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1104,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 276,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
