{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e001","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b194-ebfd-7972-8291-a2a8c88f871f"},"sequence":3675,"recorded_at":1780531400007345,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"df48a3ca-89bc-4d9a-855b-51fcacb1bf2e"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nRev4 rework of TASK-260830-1geqhj is complete on base `2fc6d50` (verified current, no refresh needed), candidate left UNCOMMITTED, handoff accepted with checklist 19/19.\n\nWhat changed (all in `internal/axpane/`, plus additive README/LOGBOOK):\n\n- **P1-1, both sites together:** deleted the `leaseCheckpointAgrees` equality; the fold is now the sole newest authority with the single implication \"checkpoint-carrying winner ⇒ published newest\" asserted once directly after fencing in `Decide` (parks `restore_policy` on a null fold, launch and restore alike). `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required → fold newest → head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; the unknown-store guard keys on the published newest. Re-pinned: post-takeover positive through `Decide` and `Run` (restore launches with C1's closure), stale-base negative, successor-null-fold negative, and wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\n- **P2-1:** `Supersede`/`installPair` now report the commit-race replay (`(Binding, bool, error)`), and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach` with the recorded receipt, pinned via the `AfterStage` hook.\n- **P3:** added the P3-1/P3-2 `Run` negatives with harness rows; re-derived the ratio (43/43, every named test verified present via `go test -list`); results report the configured 27 commands verbatim; matrix phantom names replaced with real drivers; P3-6 stated as a classification-only bound; P3-7 binds the identity record's `session_id` (foreign record refuses `invalid_config`); stale README/TRACEABILITY/LOGBOOK prose corrected (rev3 LOGBOOK carries an explicit REVERSAL paragraph).\n\nEvidence: full configured 27-command suite green (race gate exit 0, 38/38, no data races; axpane 192 PASS, 80.9% cover), mutant harness 53/53 on two passes (52 KILLED + control) with per-plant raw logs, packaged as a real gzip. Attached: `TASK-260830-1geqhj_results-rev4.md`, `TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix-rev4.md`, `TASK-260830-1geqhj_rev4-evidence.tar.gz`. `internal/traceability` untouched.","reason":null}}
